WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正专为你制作《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.260
That's us.
就是我们。

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.020
Hey there.
嘿，大家好。

10
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:25.980
We are here.
我们到了。

11
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.360
We are here, and we're excited because today we're talking about Hot Girl.
我们到了，而且很兴奋，因为今天我们要聊的是《辣妹》这一集。

12
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.340
Hot Girl Season 1, Episode 6, written by Mindy Kaling and directed by Amy Heckerling.
《辣妹》，第一季第六集，由敏迪·卡灵编剧，艾米·海克林执导。

13
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.500
I was really excited to meet Amy Heckerling.
我当时真的很兴奋能见到艾米·海克林。

14
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.140
You know, growing up, guys, I might be a child of the 70s.
你们知道的，伙计们，我成长在70年代。

15
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.420
No judgment, the oldie sitting here.
别评判我，这儿坐着个老古董呢。

16
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.040
No, and she directed Fast Times at Ridgemont High and Clueless.
不，她可是执导了《开放的美国学府》和《独领风骚》的人。

17
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:48.800
Clueless.
《独领风骚》。

18
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.320
Clueless.
《独领风骚》。

19
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.120
So I was excited.
所以我很兴奋。

20
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.900
I remember there was a bit of a buzz.
我记得当时引起了一些轰动。

21
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.040
Yeah, there was a little bit of a buzz.
没错，确实引起了一点轰动。

22
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.800
That she was coming in.
因为她要来了。

23
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.640
We were very excited.
我们当时非常兴奋。

24
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.260
I didn't know how to make small talk with her.
我不知道该怎么跟她寒暄。

25
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:56.820
And guess what?
结果呢？

26
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.460
I failed.
我失败了。

27
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.860
All right, Jenna, hit us with a synopsis.
好了，珍娜，给我们讲讲剧情梗概吧。

28
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.760
All right, synopsis of this episode.
好的，这一集的剧情梗概。

29
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.360
Michael allows a woman selling purses to set up in the conference room for the day,
迈克尔允许一名卖手提包的女士在会议室摆摊一天，

30
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.780
and Michael and Dwight compete for her attention.
迈克尔和德怀特为了博取她的关注展开了竞争。

31
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.300
Very simple.
非常简单。

32
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.220
Very simple.
非常简单。

33
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:12.980
And yet...
然而……

34
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.340
So loaded for Pam.
对帕姆来说信息量很大。

35
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.860
This was really a big Pam episode.
这确实是帕姆戏份很重的一集。

36
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.180
It really was.
确实如此。

37
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.080
So should we start with some fast facts then?
那我们先从一些速览事实开始吧？

38
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.180
I know you want to.
我知道你想说。

39
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:21.700
You know.
你懂的。

40
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.960
My fast fact, number one, this is the first episode written by Mindy Kaling.
我的第一个速览事实，这是敏迪·卡灵编剧的第一集。

41
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.620
Yes, Mindy Kaling's so smart, so funny.
没错，敏迪·卡灵太聪明、太有趣了。

42
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.160
And she was one of our most prolific writers on The Office.
她是《办公室》里最高产的编剧之一。

43
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.280
She wrote a total of, Jenna, ready?
她总共写了，珍娜，准备好了吗？

44
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:33.820
What?
什么？

45
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.320
22 episodes.
22集。

46
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.100
Wow.
哇。

47
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:36.840
I know.
我知道。

48
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.820
That's like she wrote an entire season of The Office.
这相当于她写了整整一季的《办公室》。

49
00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:40.200
I know.
我知道。

50
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.680
Of our nine, because the season's usually about 22, 24 episodes.
我们一共九季，因为每一季通常大约是22到24集。

51
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.680
I have a fan question about Mindy.
我有一个关于敏迪的粉丝提问。

52
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.220
All right.
好的。

53
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.100
This is from Bear.
这是来自贝尔的提问。

54
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:47.860
Hi, Bear.
你好，贝尔。

55
00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.120
Yes, Bear asked,
没错，贝尔问的是，

56
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.440
this episode was written by Mindy Kaling.
这一集是由敏迪·卡灵编剧的。

57
00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.620
What was it like to work with her as a writer versus an actor?
作为编剧和作为演员，与她共事有什么不同？

58
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.240
Oh, Bear, good question.
噢，贝尔，好问题。

59
00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:56.840
I know.
我知道。

60
00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.920
Oh, you know what?
噢，你知道吗？

61
00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.120
I loved when Mindy was the writer of the episode,
我喜欢敏迪担任编剧的那几集，

62
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.820
because the writer of the episode on our show would stay on set all week
因为我们剧的编剧会整周待在片场，

63
00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.700
and produce their episode with the director.
并与导演一起制作他们负责的那一集。

64
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.160
So they kind of worked very side by side with the director.
所以他们基本上是与导演并肩作战的。

65
00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.800
Yes, and they were sort of the liaison back to the writer's room.
是的，他们也算是与编剧室沟通的联络人。

66
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.220
I love that our show did this.
我喜欢我们剧组这种做法。

67
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.380
Not all shows do that.
并非所有剧组都这样做。

68
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.460
And I really think you benefit from having the writer of the episode on the set with you.
而且我真的认为，有编剧在片场陪着你，你会受益匪浅。

69
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.780
Well, Mindy, it was so easy to make Mindy laugh.
嗯，敏迪，逗笑敏迪太容易了。

70
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.640
Like, she was so ready to love everything you were doing.
她总是准备好去喜欢你所做的一切。

71
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.600
You were filled with such confidence when Mindy was on the set.
当敏迪在片场时，你会感到信心十足。

72
00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:34.240
And she also was really good on the spot coming up with new jokes,
而且她非常擅长现场想出新笑话，

73
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.760
because that was another thing that the writer of the episode would do.
因为这也是该集编剧会做的事情之一。

74
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.880
They would pitch you improvisations on the spot.
他们会当场为你提供即兴创作的建议。

75
00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:41.380
Yeah.
是的。

76
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.880
And Mindy, for me, as someone with like an improv background,
而对于我这种有即兴表演背景的人来说，

77
00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.740
I loved being able to pitch to Mindy because she's so smart.
我喜欢向敏迪提出建议，因为她太聪明了。

78
00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.800
So I could like say, hey, Mindy, could I, you know, try this?
所以我可以问，嘿，敏迪，我能试试这个吗？

79
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.080
And then she would just instantly be like, oh, that'd be great.
然后她会立刻说，噢，那太棒了。

80
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:52.960
Or how about you do this?
或者说，你试试这样做怎么样？

81
00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.080
Like, she was such a wonderful, creative collaborator.
她真是一位出色的创意合作伙伴。

82
00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.860
I always felt like Mindy was such a big advocate for the character of Pam as well.
我一直觉得敏迪也是帕姆这个角色的坚定支持者。

83
00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.360
I think she was in the writer's room pitching storylines for Pam.
我想她在编剧室里为帕姆构思过剧情。

84
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.540
And this was a very Pam-centered episode, as we said.
正如我们所说，这一集是以帕姆为核心的。

85
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.240
Pam has feelings.
帕姆是有感情的。

86
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.520
She has a lot of feelings.
她有很多感情。

87
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.140
Pam has a lot of feelings.
帕姆确实有很多感情。

88
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:11.820
She does.
她确实有。

89
00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.220
This leads me into my second fastback.
这引出了我的第二个快问快答。

90
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.300
I was texting with Mindy about this episode in preparation.
为了准备这一集，我一直在和敏迪发短信。

91
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.320
And she told me something.
她告诉了我一件事。

92
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:19.940
What?
什么事？

93
00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.940
The original title of this episode was Purse Girl.
这一集的最初标题是《卖包女孩》。

94
00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:23.700
Oh.
噢。

95
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.440
Do you kind of remember that?
你还记得吗？

96
00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.780
I actually do because I feel like I have referred to this as Purse Girl a few times
我确实记得，因为我觉得我好几次都把它称为《卖包女孩》，

97
00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.600
because it's in my brain.
因为它已经印在我的脑海里了。

98
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:30.940
Yeah.
是的。

99
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.880
She also told me that her original draft of this was 39 pages.
她还告诉我，她最初的剧本草稿有39页。

100
00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.100
Wow.
哇。

101
00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.440
Which is a lot because usually the number of pages that a script is,
这可是相当长的篇幅，因为通常剧本的页数，

102
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:42.400
that's how many minutes of screen time it is.
就代表了屏幕上的时长。

103
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.380
So her script, if we did it exactly as written, would have been 39 minutes,
所以她的剧本，如果我们完全照着拍，会有39分钟，

104
00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.600
which we would not have been able to air.
那是我们无法播出的长度。

105
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.160
I really wish we could have done that.
我真希望我们能那样做。

106
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.440
And I wish we could have filmed all 40 pages of that instead of 22, 22 minutes.
我真希望我们能把那40页全部拍出来，而不是22分钟的版本。

107
00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.840
I remember they used to have those very long table drafts and then they would cut a bunch
我记得以前他们会有那种非常长的剧本初稿，然后会删掉一大堆内容，

108
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.500
of stuff out and they would make something they called the candy bag.
把删掉的东西做成一个他们称之为“糖果袋”的东西。

109
00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:01.800
Yeah.
没错。

110
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.380
And those were all of the cut scenes or they were additional takes on scenes.
那些都是被删掉的场景，或者是场景的额外拍摄片段。

111
00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:12.380
So whatever talking head wound up in the script, there would be five different takes on that
所以无论最终剧本里留下了哪个采访镜头，在“糖果袋”里都会有五个不同的版本。

112
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.860
talking head in the candy bag.
那个采访镜头。

113
00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.560
And so we would sit down to do our talking heads and they would say, all right, well,
所以当我们坐下来准备拍采访镜头时，他们会说，好吧，

114
00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:21.320
we're going to do the scripted one, but then we're going to do three of them from the candy bag.
我们要拍剧本里的那个，但之后还要从“糖果袋”里再拍三个。

115
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.580
Oh, I remember going to do a talking head and they handed me three pages of alts,
哦，我记得有一次去拍采访镜头，他们直接递给我三页纸的备选台词，

116
00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.780
like right in the minute.
就在那一分钟里。

117
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.520
I'm like, oh, right.
我当时心想，哦，好吧。

118
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:27.900
Okay.
行吧。

119
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.280
I'm going to have to have a photographic memory.
我得有照相机般的记忆力才行。

120
00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.800
You have to really be on your toes.
你真的得时刻保持警惕。

121
00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.080
I think that's something that-
我觉得那是……

122
00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.600
It kept us on our toes for sure.
那确实让我们时刻保持警惕。

123
00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.580
I loved it.
我很喜欢那样。

124
00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.420
I loved it too.
我也很喜欢。

125
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.360
And then they used to let me play around and like,
而且他们以前还会让我自由发挥，

126
00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.900
sort of like put my spin on it too, which was always fun.
加入我自己的风格，这总是很有趣。

127
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.600
All right, Fisher, what else you got?
好了，费舍尔，你还有什么？

128
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.140
All right.
好的。

129
00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.440
I think it's time to talk about Amy AdaMs.
我觉得是时候聊聊艾米·亚当斯了。

130
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.040
Okay.
好的。

131
00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.500
I have a lot of note cards here in front of me.
我面前有很多笔记卡片。

132
00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.100
I see.
我看到了。

133
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.140
And a lot of them have the words Amy or Amy Adams on them.
而且其中很多上面都写着“艾米”或“艾米·亚当斯”。

134
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.060
You tell me when you're ready because I've got a note card ready to go.
你准备好了就告诉我，因为我已经准备好一张笔记卡片了。

135
00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.980
Well, this is our third fast fact.
嗯，这是我们的第三个速记事实。

136
00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.840
Amy Adams was the purse girl.
艾米·亚当斯演过“包包女孩”。

137
00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:03.460
Mindy told me that Amy was her favorite from the very beginning.
敏迪告诉我，艾米从一开始就是她最喜欢的演员。

138
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.060
This is who she wanted to cast as the purse girl from her audition.
这就是她从试镜中选定要演“包包女孩”的人。

139
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:13.200
But something that I think people don't realize is that Amy Adams wasn't Amy Adams when she was cast as the purse girl.
但我觉得人们没意识到的一点是，艾米·亚当斯在被选为“包包女孩”时，还不是后来那个艾米·亚当斯。

140
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.720
She became Amy Adams later.
她是后来才成为艾米·亚当斯的。

141
00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:21.160
And that's an interesting story, actually, because we filmed this episode in the fall of 2004,
说实话，这其实是个有趣的故事，因为我们是在2004年秋天拍摄的那集，

142
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.120
but they didn't start airing until the spring of 2005.
但直到2005年春天才开始播出。

143
00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:30.680
And that fall, she was nominated for an Academy Award for her role in Junebug.
而那年秋天，她凭借在《甲壳虫》中的角色获得了奥斯卡提名。

144
00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.000
Right.
没错。

145
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:36.660
When she did this episode of The Office, no one had seen Junebug yet because Junebug came out in August of 2005.
当她拍《办公室》这一集时，还没人看过《甲壳虫》，因为《甲壳虫》是2005年8月才上映的。

146
00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:37.080
Yes.
是的。

147
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:41.660
And I remember her first day on set, we were talking, and I was like, how are things going?
我记得她第一天到片场时，我们聊天，我问她，最近怎么样？

148
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.920
She's like, well, you know, it's good.
她说，嗯，你知道，还不错。

149
00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.780
I mean, I was on a show on CBS called Dr. Vegas, but they let me go.
我是说，我之前在CBS的一部叫《拉斯维加斯医生》的剧里演过，但他们把我解雇了。

150
00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.160
Oh, that's right.
哦，对哦。

151
00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.780
She was like, I kind of got fired.
她说，我好像被解雇了。

152
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.540
And I was like, no.
我说，不会吧。

153
00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.300
And she was like, yeah.
她说，是真的。

154
00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.600
And I was really down, and I was bummed out.
我当时真的很沮丧，心情很低落。

155
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:59.780
But then, you know, I did this little indie movie called Junebug, and I feel so good about it.
但后来，你知道，我拍了一部叫《甲壳虫》的小成本独立电影，我对它感觉非常好。

156
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.260
And it's going to come out later in the year.
它会在今年晚些时候上映。

157
00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.760
And I was like, oh, that sounds great.
我说，哦，那听起来太棒了。

158
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:03.340
Yeah.
是啊。

159
00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.000
Let me build you up, Amy AdaMs.
让我来鼓励一下你，艾米·亚当斯。

160
00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.160
Amy, you're going to be just fine.
艾米，你会没事的。

161
00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.080
And she was.
她确实没事。

162
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:09.640
And she was.
她确实没事。

163
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.040
But Amy is one of the nicest people.
但艾米是最好的人之一。

164
00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.120
She's so, so sweet.
她真的非常非常贴心。

165
00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.600
Oh, I loved Amy.
哦，我太喜欢艾米了。

166
00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.780
It was so fun working with her.
和她一起工作太有趣了。

167
00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:24.240
There were a lot of questions from fans asking if we planned to bring this character back after we shot it.
拍摄结束后，很多粉丝问我们是否计划让这个角色回归。

168
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.180
Well, we didn't think we were going to have a show.
嗯，我们当时没想过这剧能成。

169
00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:26.660
Right.
没错。

170
00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.720
There were no real plans to bring her back.
本来确实没打算让她回归。

171
00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.120
But then when the show got picked up, they wanted to bring her back.
但后来剧集被续订了，他们就想让她回来。

172
00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.160
But now she was Academy Award nominated Amy AdaMs.
可那时候她已经是获得奥斯卡提名的艾米·亚当斯了。

173
00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.820
I was like, well, I hope we can get her back.
我心想，好吧，希望我们能请回她。

174
00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:39.360
And we did.
我们确实做到了。

175
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.800
And she came back for two more episodes.
她又回来拍了两集。

176
00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:41.380
Yes.
是的。

177
00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.800
And she was such a great foil, too, for Pam and Jim and all of that.
而且她和帕姆、吉姆他们搭戏时，表现得非常出彩。

178
00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.240
I loved watching that play out.
我很喜欢看那段剧情的发展。

179
00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:55.420
Not only was Amy Adams super nice on set and just, like, such a pleasure to work with, but, I don't know, probably, like, two years later, I ran into her.
艾米·亚当斯不仅在片场人超级好，合作起来非常愉快，而且，我不知道，大概两年后，我偶遇了她。

180
00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.380
I had a friend visiting from Alabama.
当时有个朋友从阿拉巴马州来看我。

181
00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.260
And you guys, I don't ever go out.
你们知道的，我平时从不出门。

182
00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.600
So my friend was coming in town.
所以朋友要来城里了。

183
00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.820
And I was like, oh, I'm going to take her somewhere fancy.
我就想，哦，我要带她去个高档的地方。

184
00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.680
That hotel, Chateau Marmont, that's fancy.
那个酒店，马尔蒙庄园酒店，那儿很高级。

185
00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:07.400
We'll go there.
我们就去那儿吧。

186
00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.500
Because I just had it in my head.
因为我脑子里就认准了那里。

187
00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.420
Yeah, like the Hollywood fancy place to eat.
对，就像好莱坞那种高档餐厅。

188
00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:10.840
It was a fancy place.
那确实是个高档地方。

189
00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:11.060
Yeah.
是啊。

190
00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.700
I mean, it's like half an hour from my house.
我是说，离我家大概半小时车程。

191
00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:13.900
It was such a, like, haul.
那可真是一段长途跋涉。

192
00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.080
But I was like, no, I'll take my friend from Alabama there.
但我还是想，不，我要带我阿拉巴马的朋友去那儿。

193
00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.060
So we went.
于是我们就去了。

194
00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.720
And we were having dinner.
我们正在吃晚餐。

195
00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.920
And Amy Adams was at a table.
艾米·亚当斯也在那儿用餐。

196
00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.820
And she sent over two glasses of champagne to my friend and I.
她给我们俩送了两杯香槟过来。

197
00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.180
And I was like, they were like, oh, this is so classy.
我当时就觉得，她们说，哦，这太有格调了。

198
00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.180
Classy move, Amy AdaMs.
真有格调，艾米·亚当斯。

199
00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:28.730
So classy.
太有格调了。

200
00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.980
And they were like, I was like, who's this from?
她们当时问，我问，这是谁送的？

201
00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.640
They were like, it's from Amy AdaMs.
他们当时说，这是艾米·亚当斯送的。

202
00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:32.820
And she waved.
然后她挥了挥手。

203
00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.100
And then she came over and we chatted.
接着她走过来，我们聊了会儿。

204
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.880
Amy Adams is just a class act.
艾米·亚当斯真是个很有风度的人。

205
00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:40.200
I have a funny Amy Adams story about how people think that we look alike.
关于人们觉得我和艾米·亚当斯长得像，我有个有趣的经历。

206
00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.880
So she and I were both at this work party thing.
当时我们俩都在参加一个工作聚会之类的活动。

207
00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.160
I can't remember exactly.
具体我也记不清了。

208
00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.160
I think it was like honoring directors in the industry.
好像是向业内导演致敬之类的活动。

209
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.260
And we were both there.
我们俩都在场。

210
00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.000
And my friend came up to me.
然后我朋友走过来找我。

211
00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.740
And he said, I am so humiliated right now.
他说，我现在真是尴尬透了。

212
00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.300
And I said, what happened?
我说，怎么了？

213
00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:01.860
And he goes, I just went up and bear hugged Amy Adams and said, Jenna, you look beautiful.
他说，我刚才走过去给了艾米·亚当斯一个熊抱，还说，珍娜，你今天真漂亮。

214
00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:02.620
Oh, no.
天哪。

215
00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.980
Because he mixed us up.
因为他把我们认错了。

216
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.120
And people have this thing where they think she and I look a lot alike.
人们总觉得我和她长得很像。

217
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.840
We really don't look anything alike in person.
其实我们本人长得一点都不像。

218
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.140
Although I guess I just told a story about someone who mixed us up in person.
虽然我刚才讲的故事里，那个人确实是当面把我们认错了。

219
00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.680
I mean, there is a resemblance.
我是说，确实有几分相似。

220
00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.140
She's perfectly cast because there is a resemblance.
选她来演很合适，因为确实有相似之处。

221
00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.840
And you're both like beautiful ladies.
而且你们都是大美女。

222
00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:20.440
Thanks.
谢谢。

223
00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.420
But I see a resemblance.
但我确实觉得有相似之处。

224
00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.760
I feel like we could play sisters.
我觉得我们可以演姐妹。

225
00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:24.640
You could.
你们确实可以。

226
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:25.720
All right, Hollywood.
好了，好莱坞。

227
00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:26.920
You heard it here firSt.
你们在这里先听到了。

228
00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.640
I guess that's how I talk when I'm talking to Hollywood.
看来我和好莱坞对话时就是这种语气。

229
00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:30.560
I guess it is.
看来确实是。

230
00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:31.880
Hollywood beware.
好莱坞小心了。

231
00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:32.700
Hollywood.
好莱坞。

232
00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.720
This is Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

233
00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:35.760
I don't love it.
我不喜欢这个语气。

234
00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.650
I think your character, your Hollywood voice lady.
我觉得你那个角色，你那个好莱坞名媛的腔调。

235
00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.590
I think you should work on it.
我觉得你应该再练练。

236
00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.010
Okay, thanks.
好吧，谢谢。

237
00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:43.750
Give it an accent.
加点口音进去。

238
00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:44.070
Oh.
噢。

239
00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.010
Should it be British?
要用英式口音吗？

240
00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:46.210
Hollywood.
好莱坞。

241
00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:46.910
No.
不。

242
00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:47.470
Oh, my God.
天哪。

243
00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.550
Oh, that's Australian.
噢，那是澳大利亚口音。

244
00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.330
Oh, what was that?
噢，刚才那是啥？

245
00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:51.870
I can't do.
我做不到。

246
00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:53.270
That was like drunk Scottish.
那听起来像喝醉了的苏格兰人。

247
00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:54.330
What is happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

248
00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:55.710
I can't do accents.
我学不会口音。

249
00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:56.990
And I also can't sing.
而且我也不会唱歌。

250
00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:00.230
I can do Australian, but I grew up overseas and all my best friends were Aussies.
我会说澳大利亚口音，因为我是在海外长大的，我最好的朋友都是澳大利亚人。

251
00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.950
So, right, now I'm just sitting here talking to Jenna.
好了，现在我正坐在这儿和珍娜聊天。

252
00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:04.770
We're going to talk about Hot Girl.
我们要聊聊《辣妹》。

253
00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:05.230
Yeah.
没错。

254
00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:06.590
That's really good, Ange.
那真的很棒，安吉。

255
00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.150
Oh, thanks.
噢，谢谢。

256
00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.270
Thanks so much.
太感谢了。

257
00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:09.950
I'm shocked.
我惊呆了。

258
00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:11.570
I'm genuinely impressed.
我是真心感到佩服。

259
00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:12.670
Okay, okay, okay.
好，好，好。

260
00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.710
See, that was so good, but your Hollywood voice is a no.
你看，刚才那段很好，但你那种好莱坞式的腔调不行。

261
00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:16.210
I know.
我知道。

262
00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:16.770
You know what?
你知道吗？

263
00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.350
It's whenever I'm trying to be slick.
每当我试图表现得圆滑时就会这样。

264
00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.590
I'm just not programmed to be slick.
我天生就不是那种圆滑的人。

265
00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.310
This is true about you.
这点你说得对。

266
00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:23.890
I know.
我知道。

267
00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:29.130
Before we go to a break, since we're talking about Amy Adams and how wonderful she is both
在休息之前，既然我们聊到了艾米·亚当斯，聊到她无论在片场内外都那么出色，

268
00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:33.850
on and off set, we have to tell the story about how she helped us meet Meryl Streep.
我们必须讲讲她是如何帮我们见到梅丽尔·斯特里普的故事。

269
00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.090
Oh, my God.
天哪。

270
00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:35.910
Oh, my God.
天哪。

271
00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.070
I cannot believe I didn't put that on a note card.
真不敢相信我竟然没把这事写在提示卡上。

272
00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:38.990
I can't believe it either.
我也真不敢相信。

273
00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:39.810
What is wrong with me?
我这是怎么了？

274
00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:40.170
You know what?
你知道吗？

275
00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:40.590
I don't know.
我也不知道。

276
00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.190
I got here.
我到了这儿。

277
00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:41.830
There were donuts.
看到了甜甜圈。

278
00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:42.610
I got excited.
我太兴奋了。

279
00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:43.190
I forgot.
就给忘了。

280
00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:43.730
Okay.
好吧。

281
00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:47.610
So, one year, we got to go to the Golden Globes.
所以，有一年，我们有机会去了金球奖颁奖典礼。

282
00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.030
Oh.
噢。

283
00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:50.190
The office had been nominated.
《办公室》获得了提名。

284
00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:56.590
And I have to say, first of all, Angela, I am so grateful that I got to go to these
我得先说，安吉拉，我真的很感激能和你一起去参加这些

285
00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.090
award show things with you.
颁奖典礼之类的活动。

286
00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:58.950
I know.
我知道。

287
00:09:59.010 --> 00:09:59.850
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，是这样的。

288
00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.930
We didn't go to fancy parties, you guys.
我们可没去参加什么高级派对，各位。

289
00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.910
We're not fancy people.
我们不是那种爱赶时髦的人。

290
00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.850
I'm intimate dinner party person.
我更喜欢私密的晚宴。

291
00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:05.710
Well, I-
嗯，我——

292
00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:06.850
I like a small group.
我喜欢小团体。

293
00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:10.470
I think the fanciest parties I'd ever been to were just like my-
我想我参加过最隆重的派对，也就是我——

294
00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.250
when one of my friends would have a big wedding.
我朋友举办盛大婚礼的时候。

295
00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:17.130
But I am so glad that I got to navigate all that stuff with you because I would normally
但我很高兴能和你一起应对那些场合，因为通常情况下，

296
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.230
kind of freeze up at something like that.
在那样的环境下我会有点不知所措。

297
00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.650
But I was there with my BFF.
但当时有我最好的朋友在身边。

298
00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.190
We would have a couple glasses of wine.
我们会喝上几杯葡萄酒。

299
00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:26.470
We would sometimes get a little-
有时还会有点——

300
00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:30.350
Well, because one thing we should say is we were not allowed to bring a plus one.
嗯，因为有一点我们得说明，那就是我们当时是不允许带家属的。

301
00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.830
Well, we were not big time enough.
好吧，我们当时还不够大牌。

302
00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:33.230
No.
没错。

303
00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.370
I feel like we were barely invited.
我觉得我们简直像是勉强被邀请的。

304
00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:36.590
Truth be told.
说实话。

305
00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.830
Even though our show was nominated, it did feel like that.
尽管我们的剧获得了提名，但感觉确实如此。

306
00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:40.890
Well, first of all-
嗯，首先——

307
00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.410
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

308
00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:41.650
What?
怎么了？

309
00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.370
Do you remember where our table was?
你还记得我们的桌子在哪吗？

310
00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:44.730
Very far away from the stage.
离舞台非常远。

311
00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.110
Our table was behind a pillar, Jenna.
我们的桌子在柱子后面，珍娜。

312
00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:48.710
I do remember that.
我确实记得。

313
00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:54.110
I had to sort of lean all the way towards Brian's lap to see the stage.
我得整个人探身凑到布莱恩的大腿边才能看到舞台。

314
00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:54.710
Yeah.
是啊。

315
00:10:55.010 --> 00:11:00.890
So the Golden Globes are really cool because they have awards for both movies and television.
金球奖真的很棒，因为他们既颁发电影奖项也颁发电视奖项。

316
00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.550
There are cool movie stars you see.
你能见到很酷的电影明星。

317
00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:10.470
As TV people, we were in the room with Angelina Jolie suddenly and Brad Pitt and all those people.
作为电视圈的人，我们突然就和安吉丽娜·朱莉、布拉德·皮特还有那些人处在同一个房间里了。

318
00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.950
We were nowhere near them, though.
不过我们离他们很远。

319
00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.750
They were down at the front, and we were in the nosebleeds.
他们坐在前排，而我们坐在山顶看台。

320
00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.210
But hey, we were in the room.
但嘿，我们好歹在现场。

321
00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:21.750
Well, I will say, I remember going to the bathroom and Angelina Jolie passed by.
嗯，我得说，我记得我去洗手间时，安吉丽娜·朱莉从旁边经过。

322
00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:23.690
She took my breath away.
她让我屏住了呼吸。

323
00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.410
I thought, well, now she is from the gods.
我想，好吧，她简直是天神下凡。

324
00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:27.470
I get that.
我懂那种感觉。

325
00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:29.150
I mean, that is a movie star.
我是说，那才是电影明星。

326
00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:34.790
Well, you turned to me because we were in line for the bathroom, and she just sort of, it's like she glided.
当时我们在排队上洗手间，你转过头对我说，她简直像是飘过去的。

327
00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:39.430
It's like she floated past us, and you turned to me and you go, now that's a movie star.
就像从我们身边滑过一样，你转过头对我说，那才叫电影明星。

328
00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:39.970
I did.
我确实说了。

329
00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.130
I sound like an old lady.
我听起来像个老太太。

330
00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.990
Now that is a movie star.
那才叫电影明星。

331
00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.350
I was like, I don't disagree, Jenna.
我当时心想，我没法反驳，珍娜。

332
00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:48.710
So Jenna and I are not two people that are invited to a lot of fancy parties.
所以我和珍娜并不是那种会受邀参加很多高档派对的人。

333
00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:54.430
And also, if there are going to be two dorks at a party, chances are they're us.
而且，如果派对上有两个书呆子，那大概率就是我们。

334
00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.090
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

335
00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:55.930
That's just us anywhere.
无论在哪我们都是这样。

336
00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.350
We've done some real dorky things at parties.
我们在派对上做过不少傻事。

337
00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:00.470
We are just kind of dorks, even if it's just like at our neighbor's barbecue.
我们就是那种书呆子，哪怕只是在邻居的烧烤聚会上。

338
00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:05.550
I was glad I got to go to those parties with you because I knew you felt as awkward at them as I did.
我很高兴能和你一起参加那些派对，因为我知道你和我一样感到尴尬。

339
00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.110
But you are way braver than I am.
但你比我勇敢得多。

340
00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.130
Way braver.
勇敢得多。

341
00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:09.590
That is true.
那是真的。

342
00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:17.910
I have a little bit of my mom's voice in my ear, and my mom would say, if you are at a fancy party, you need to meet the fancy people.
我脑子里总会响起我妈妈的声音，她会说，如果你参加高档派对，你就得去结识那些大人物。

343
00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:20.310
You need to use it as an opportunity.
你得利用这个机会。

344
00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:20.930
Come on.
加油。

345
00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.910
Go say hi to the people you want to say hi to.
去跟你想打招呼的人打个招呼。

346
00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:28.590
So I always have that in the back of my head, like, this is my only chance to whatever.
所以我脑子里总有这个念头，觉得这是我唯一的机会去干什么。

347
00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:29.250
Hobnob?
去攀谈？

348
00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:32.310
Yeah, meet whoever I've always wanted to meet, I guess.
对，去见见那些我一直想见的人，我想是吧。

349
00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.210
But what do you do?
但你该怎么做呢？

350
00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:36.490
How do you get into the conversation is always the mystery.
如何加入对话一直是个谜。

351
00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.950
So at this Golden Globes...
在这次金球奖颁奖典礼上……

352
00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.310
I'm starting to laugh.
我开始笑了。

353
00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.670
We had our in.
我们找到了机会。

354
00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:46.850
We look across the room, and we see Amy Adams talking to Meryl Streit.
我们看向房间对面，看到艾米·亚当斯在和梅丽尔·斯特里普聊天。

355
00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:52.190
We lean around the pillar we're sitting behind, and we see Amy AdaMs.
我们从坐着的柱子后面探出头，看到了艾米·亚当斯。

356
00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.730
You should know at this point, we'd been sitting at our table for quite a while.
你们要知道，当时我们在桌边已经坐了很久了。

357
00:12:55.870 --> 00:13:00.690
We hadn't got up and mingled other than we went to the bathroom and saw Angelina Jolie walk by, and we didn't say a word.
除了去洗手间时看到安吉丽娜·朱莉走过，我们一句话也没说，也没去和别人寒暄。

358
00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:01.690
No, I did not speak to her.
不，我没跟她说话。

359
00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:02.430
We did not speak to her.
我们没跟她说话。

360
00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.250
So Jenna's like, there's Amy AdaMs.
所以珍娜说，看，那是艾米·亚当斯。

361
00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.790
And Angela, she's talking to Meryl Streit.
而且安吉拉，她在和梅丽尔·斯特里普聊天。

362
00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:06.950
We know Amy AdaMs.
我们认识艾米·亚当斯。

363
00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:07.310
Yes.
是的。

364
00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:08.670
We can go talk to Amy AdaMs.
我们可以过去跟艾米·亚当斯打招呼。

365
00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:09.350
We know her.
我们认识她。

366
00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:10.190
She likes us.
她喜欢我们。

367
00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.630
And Jenna was like, come on, Angela, let's go.
珍娜就说，来吧，安吉拉，我们走。

368
00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:19.790
And I was like, nope, don't want to go.
我说，不，我不想去。

369
00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:20.430
Not going.
不去。

370
00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:20.910
Not going.
不去。

371
00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.170
And you really, like, you were like, Angela?
你当时真的很惊讶，你问我，安吉拉？

372
00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:24.490
I pulled you from the table.
我把你从桌边拉了起来。

373
00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.410
I said, we are meeting Meryl Streit.
我说，我们要去见梅丽尔·斯特里普。

374
00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:27.550
We are doing this.
我们一定要去。

375
00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.110
This is a story for my mother.
这可是能讲给我妈听的故事。

376
00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:29.710
Come on.
走吧。

377
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.730
And then she said, and you got to be quick.
然后她说，你得快点。

378
00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.370
You have to be quick, because what if Amy stops talking to her?
你必须快点，万一艾米不跟她聊了怎么办？

379
00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:36.210
Yeah, let's go.
好，我们走。

380
00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.370
And you said, well, what are we going to do?
然后你问，好吧，我们要怎么做？

381
00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:39.190
What are we going to say?
我们要说什么？

382
00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:40.710
How do you walk up to them?
怎么走过去找她们？

383
00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:41.470
What are we going to say?
我们要说什么？

384
00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.930
So I was like, here is my plan.
我就说，我的计划是这样的。

385
00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.030
We are just going to walk up to them laughing.
我们直接笑着走过去。

386
00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:46.150
What?
什么？

387
00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:47.690
Just laugh.
就笑。

388
00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:48.270
What?
什么？

389
00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:50.990
And I said, laugh at what?
我说，笑什么？

390
00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:51.910
It doesn't matter.
不重要。

391
00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:52.390
What are we laughing at?
我们笑什么啊？

392
00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.330
I said, it doesn't matter.
我说，那不重要。

393
00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:54.690
Just walk up to them laughing.
直接笑着走过去就行。

394
00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:57.350
I think you thought if we just walked up laughing, we would look cool.
我想你当时觉得，如果我们笑着走过去，看起来会很酷。

395
00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.570
Like, we're like, I don't know what I thought, Angela.
就像，我们……我不知道我当时在想什么，安吉拉。

396
00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

397
00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.330
I just knew we had to seize the moment.
我只知道我们必须抓住时机。

398
00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.190
So we did.
所以我们就去了。

399
00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:08.250
Well, I said, I basically was like in shock.
好吧，我说，我当时基本上处于震惊状态。

400
00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.230
I was like, wait, wait, what?
我说，等等，等等，什么？

401
00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:09.590
What, what?
什么，什么？

402
00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:12.650
And then I looked, and Jenna was like four strides away.
然后我一看，珍娜大概离我有四步远。

403
00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:13.690
Like, kind of like.
就像，差不多吧。

404
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:13.990
I committed.
我下定决心了。

405
00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.110
You're like, come on.
你就像在说，来吧。

406
00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:18.730
And then I sort of half-ass committed behind you.
然后我有点敷衍地跟在你后面下定决心了。

407
00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.330
And we did just that.
我们真的就那么做了。

408
00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.830
We walked up to Meryl Streep and Amy Adams laughing.
我们笑着走向梅丽尔·斯特里普和艾米·亚当斯。

409
00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:29.310
And right at that moment, a house photographer came by and snapped our photo.
就在那一刻，一位现场摄影师走过来拍下了我们的照片。

410
00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.150
So we have a photo of us.
所以我们有一张合影。

411
00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:36.290
And it looks like we are having a hilarious conversation with Meryl Streep and Amy AdaMs.
看起来就像我们正在和梅丽尔·斯特里普以及艾米·亚当斯进行一场欢快的谈话。

412
00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:42.110
Well, actually, to clarify, it looks like you and Amy and Meryl Streep are having a great conversation.
嗯，其实澄清一下，看起来是你和艾米还有梅丽尔·斯特里普在进行一场很棒的谈话。

413
00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:46.990
But because I lagged behind you a little, I was late getting there.
但因为我比你稍微落后了一点，我到的时候晚了。

414
00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.330
And I just look like I'm walking alone laughing.
我看起来就像是一个人走着在傻笑。

415
00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:54.610
I'm like a good three paces behind you laughing to no one.
我大概落后你三步远，对着空气傻笑。

416
00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.930
And you're laughing with Meryl and Amy.
而你正在和梅丽尔还有艾米谈笑风生。

417
00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:02.150
But when the lights like flickered because it was the commercial and we didn't even get to talk to them.
但当灯光闪烁时，因为那是广告时间，我们甚至没能和她们说上话。

418
00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:07.350
I did get to say to Meryl Streep, I did get to say, it's such a pleasure to meet you.
我确实对梅丽尔·斯特里普说了，我确实说了，见到您真是太荣幸了。

419
00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:09.050
I am a big admirer of your work.
我非常欣赏您的作品。

420
00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:12.750
And I was, I mean, I just loved her performance in Kramer vs. Kramer.
我是说，我太喜欢她在《克莱默夫妇》里的表演了。

421
00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.570
I studied a lot of her work.
我研究过她很多作品。

422
00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:21.370
And so as like a theater geek, actor-y person, we've talked a lot about my love of actor prep.
所以作为一个戏剧极客，一个演员类型的人，我们聊过很多关于我对比演员准备工作的热爱。

423
00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.410
That was a big moment for me.
那对我来说是一个重要的时刻。

424
00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:25.150
Well, I'm glad you had that moment.
嗯，很高兴你有过那个时刻。

425
00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.430
I did not meet her.
我没见到她。

426
00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.290
Wait, you didn't meet her?
等等，你没见到她？

427
00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:31.050
No, no, I didn't meet her because they were dimming the lights.
没有，没有，我没见到她，因为当时灯光正在调暗。

428
00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:34.530
And so the, like, by the time I got there, I was just like, bye.
所以，等我到那儿的时候，我只能说，再见。

429
00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.970
Well, she's one of my best friends now from that moment.
好吧，从那一刻起，她现在是我最好的朋友之一了。

430
00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:39.590
I've never spoken to her again.
我再也没和她说过话。

431
00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:40.930
You've never spoken to her again.
你再也没和她说过话。

432
00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:44.710
My guess is that Meryl Streep doesn't quite remember that moment the way we do.
我猜梅丽尔·斯特里普对那一刻的记忆和我们不太一样。

433
00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:45.430
I know.
我知道。

434
00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:46.730
Well, we have a photo of it.
好吧，我们有照片为证。

435
00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:47.710
We do have a photo.
我们确实有照片。

436
00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.230
All right, guys, we're going to go to a break.
好了，各位，我们要去休息一下了。

437
00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.590
And when we come back, we're going to break down the Hot Girl episode.
回来之后，我们将解析《辣妹》那一集。

438
00:15:52.950 --> 00:16:00.730
All right, this episode starts with Michael on a phone call with Jan.
好的，这一集开头是迈克尔和简在通电话。

439
00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.570
She's explaining that they're going to introduce a new incentive program.
她在解释说他们要引入一个新的激励计划。

440
00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.750
And the top seller in the office is going to get a prize worth $1,000.
办公室里销售业绩最好的人将获得一份价值1000美元的奖品。

441
00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.130
And that Michael can choose what that prize is.
而且迈克尔可以决定奖品是什么。

442
00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:11.930
The end.
结束。

443
00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:19.270
So I love that this episode starts with the line, are you listening to me, Michael?
我很喜欢这一集以“你在听我说话吗，迈克尔？”这句话开头。

444
00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.070
By Jan.
简说的。

445
00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:24.910
Because he's just, like, futzing around with pencils and he has her own speakerphone.
因为他当时只是在摆弄铅笔，而且他开着免提。

446
00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.770
But I love that the first scene, you just think he's being an idiot.
但我喜欢第一场戏，你以为他只是在犯傻。

447
00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:31.350
And then you hear this voice say, are you listening to me, Michael?
然后你听到这个声音说，你在听我说话吗，迈克尔？

448
00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.510
And I just love it.
我太喜欢这个了。

449
00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.190
I love it.
我喜欢。

450
00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:44.170
The next scene when Dwight is standing over Michael's shoulder in the talking head, it begins as a talking head and then it reveals that Dwight is kind of, like, hovering.
下一场戏，当德怀特站在迈克尔身后进行采访时，开始是采访，然后揭示出德怀特其实是在那儿徘徊。

451
00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:45.810
That's the first time we did that.
那是我们第一次那样做。

452
00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:48.610
But then we will do that many times in the show.
但之后我们在节目里会多次那样做。

453
00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:52.950
It's one of my favorite things is how Dwight stands over Michael's shoulder.
德怀特站在迈克尔肩膀后方，这是我最喜欢的桥段之一。

454
00:16:52.950 --> 00:17:01.370
That's also when Pam comes into the office to say someone wants to sell handbags and Michael is totally against it, of course, until he sees how attractive the woman is.
那也是帕姆走进办公室说有人要卖手提包的时候，迈克尔当然是坚决反对，直到他看到那个女人有多迷人。

455
00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:08.310
A lot of people wrote in and wanted to know, where did these purses come from that she's selling?
很多人写信来问，她卖的这些包是从哪儿来的？

456
00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:09.810
So I called Phil Shea.
所以我给菲尔·谢伊打了电话。

457
00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:10.730
Our prop master.
我们的道具师。

458
00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:11.190
Yes.
没错。

459
00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.430
He told me that he bought them all in downtown LA.
他告诉我，他是在洛杉矶市中心买的。

460
00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.010
Oh, at, like, the markets downtown?
哦，是在市中心的那些市场吗？

461
00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:16.610
Yes.
是的。

462
00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.470
Oh, the knockoff purse market?
哦，是卖仿冒包的市场吗？

463
00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:18.830
Yes.
是的。

464
00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:22.930
Because some of them looked really nice, but also they looked a little, like, pleather.
因为有些包看起来真的很不错，但也有点像人造革。

465
00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:24.410
I don't think anyone kept them.
我觉得没人留着它们。

466
00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:25.210
I didn't keep one.
我没留。

467
00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:25.530
Did you?
你留了吗？

468
00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:26.510
I didn't know we could.
我不知道我们能留。

469
00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:27.890
I probably would have taken one.
我当时可能会拿一个。

470
00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:32.050
It was early on when we weren't brave enough to ask to take things yet.
那是早期，我们还没胆量开口要东西。

471
00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:32.670
Yeah, no.
是啊，没要。

472
00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:37.470
