00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:31.230
Oh, so it's British when you are offended.
噢，原来你被冒犯时会带点英国口音。

533
00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:31.910
Oh, God.
天哪。

534
00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:32.810
No, stop.
不，别说了。

535
00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:33.270
Stop.
停下。

536
00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:38.490
I was just going to say that Michael Scott has a talking head that I love so much.
我只是想说，迈克尔·斯科特有个我特别喜欢的采访片段。

537
00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:43.450
And these are just one of these talking heads that they're in every episode and getting to rewatch them.
这些采访片段每集都有，重温的时候。

538
00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:45.610
I'm like, ah, my God, that's brilliant.
我就想，天哪，太精彩了。

539
00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.090
Is it the small businessman?
是关于小企业主的那段吗？

540
00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:47.990
I love it.
我超爱那个。

541
00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:48.970
Is it the things that he reads?
是他读的东西吗？

542
00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:53.210
I love that he said he loves American Way magazine, the in-flight magazine.
我特别喜欢他说他喜欢《美国之路》杂志，就是那种机上杂志。

543
00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:59.170
And then he goes, they did a great profile on Doris Roberts and where she likes to eat when she's in Phoenix.
然后他说，他们给多丽丝·罗伯茨做了一篇很棒的专访，介绍了她去菲尼克斯时喜欢去哪儿吃饭。

544
00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.230
It just made me laugh so hard because I read those.
这让我笑得不行，因为我也会看那些。

545
00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:09.130
I just want you to know American Airlines, whenever I fly with you, I get the American way out and I look to see where people eat.
我想让美国航空知道，每次我坐你们的飞机，我都会拿出《美国之路》杂志，看看别人都去哪儿吃饭。

546
00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:10.810
It made me laugh so hard.
这真的让我笑得不行。

547
00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.610
And then he's like, illuminating.
然后他说，很有启发性。

548
00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:14.650
I love those magazines, too.
我也很喜欢那些杂志。

549
00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:15.770
I read them.
我都会读。

550
00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:21.930
And, you know, actually, one of the coolest things that ever happened to me is that one time I had an article in.
而且，你知道吗，其实我经历过最酷的事情之一，就是有一次我的文章被刊登在上面。

551
00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:23.370
In an in-flight magazine?
在机上杂志里？

552
00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:23.730
Yes.
是的。

553
00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.890
Just like the Doris Roberts thing, I got profiled.
就像多丽丝·罗伯茨那件事一样，我被写进专题报道了。

554
00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:26.490
What?
什么？

555
00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.190
I would be so excited.
我会超级兴奋的。

556
00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:29.110
Why didn't you tell me?
你为什么没告诉我？

557
00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:29.890
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

558
00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:33.570
No, I told this story about playing poker in Scotland.
不，我讲的是那个在苏格兰打扑克的故事。

559
00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:35.110
Oh, wait, wait.
噢，等等，等等。

560
00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.670
I know this is a total tangent.
我知道这完全跑题了。

561
00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:37.710
Guys, I'm sorry.
伙计们，抱歉。

562
00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:40.090
I have to take Jen on a tangent because I love this story.
我得带珍跑个题，因为我太喜欢这个故事了。

563
00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.090
Yeah, should I tell the story?
是啊，我要讲这个故事吗？

564
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.210
You have to tell it.
你一定要讲。

565
00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:42.510
Okay.
好吧。

566
00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:44.970
Because, first of all, it makes you sound way cooler than you are.
因为首先，这让你听起来比实际酷多了。

567
00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:45.450
No offense.
没有冒犯的意思。

568
00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:46.010
I know.
我知道。

569
00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.650
But it kind of makes you sound like a rock star.
但这让你听起来像个摇滚明星。

570
00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.910
It's my biggest rock star moment of my life.
那是我人生中最摇滚的时刻。

571
00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:50.750
It's pretty.
挺不错的。

572
00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:51.450
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

573
00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:51.790
Okay.
好吧。

574
00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.310
So, I had no way.
当时我没别的办法。

575
00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:57.010
I know you're going to tell that story, but I need to see that in-flight magazine article.
我知道你要讲那个故事，但我得看看那本机上杂志的文章。

576
00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:57.490
I'll show it to you.
我会给你看的。

577
00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:58.730
It was for United.
那是美联航的。

578
00:20:59.050 --> 00:20:59.290
Okay.
好的。

579
00:20:59.450 --> 00:20:59.830
Magazine.
杂志。

580
00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:06.870
And they had this story where they wanted people to tell the craziest ways they've ever fought jet lag.
他们当时有个专题，想让人们分享自己克服时差最疯狂的方法。

581
00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:07.310
Okay.
好的。

582
00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:07.410
Okay.
好吧。

583
00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:11.730
So, Lee and I had this little romantic trip that we took to Scotland.
当时我和李去苏格兰进行了一次小小的浪漫旅行。

584
00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.230
This was before we had children.
那是在我们有孩子之前。

585
00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:17.910
I remember this because you told me you were going, and I was like, well, that's not a lot of days.
我记得这件事，因为你当时告诉我你们要去，我心想，那也没几天啊。

586
00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:21.750
Yeah, we only had five days because we had a one-week hiatus from work.
是啊，我们只有五天，因为工作刚好有一周的空档期。

587
00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.530
This is what people without children can do.
这就是没孩子的人能做的事。

588
00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:23.790
Yeah.
没错。

589
00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:27.670
They can just jet off to Scotland for five days.
他们可以随心所欲地飞去苏格兰玩五天。

590
00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:36.050
So, we were going to spend two days in Edinburgh, and then we were going to go into the countryside for the other three days, do a tour of, you know,
所以，我们打算在爱丁堡待两天，然后去乡下待三天，参观一下，你知道的，

591
00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:39.010
like a scotch factory and everything really fun.
比如威士忌酒厂之类的，真的很有趣。

592
00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:48.450
So, we get there, and we thought we will take an overnight flight, we will sleep on the plane, and we will arrive at noon rested and ready to tour Edinburgh.
我们到了那里，本以为坐夜航飞过去，在飞机上睡一觉，中午就能精神饱满地开始游览爱丁堡了。

593
00:21:48.730 --> 00:21:49.430
Yeah, right.
是啊，想得美。

594
00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:50.650
This did not happen.
结果根本没发生。

595
00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:53.670
We did not sleep on the plane, and we landed.
我们在飞机上没睡着，落地的时候，

596
00:21:53.890 --> 00:22:00.510
It was noon, and we were thinking, how in the world are we going to make it through this whole day?
已经是中午了，我们在想，到底该怎么撑过这一整天呢？

597
00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:01.550
You were exhausted.
你们当时精疲力竭。

598
00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:02.330
We were so tired.
我们累坏了。

599
00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:03.690
We're touring a castle.
我们当时在参观城堡。

600
00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:05.730
We're walking along little shops.
我们走在那些小店旁边。

601
00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:10.550
We bought some hats at a little hat shop.
我们在一家小帽子店买了几顶帽子。

602
00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:11.410
Oh, wait, I know.
哦，等等，我知道了。

603
00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:17.770
I know I'm raising my hand because, Jenna, you texted me, and I remember you saying, we're so tired, we're going to try to power through.
我知道我为什么要举手，因为珍娜，你给我发过短信，我记得你说过，我们太累了，但我们要试着撑过去。

604
00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:20.470
We're going to try to power through so we don't fall asleep.
我们要试着撑过去，这样就不会睡着了。

605
00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:20.850
Yes.
没错。

606
00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:22.750
In the middle, you can't fall asleep in the middle of the day.
在白天，你不能在白天睡着。

607
00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:23.450
Then you're ruined.
不然你就完了。

608
00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:27.130
Then you're, the whole five days, you're just going to be sleeping during the day and up at night.
那样的话，这五天里，你白天只会一直睡觉，晚上却醒着。

609
00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:32.630
So, it's five o'clock, and we are so exhausted, just so incredibly exhausted.
所以，当时是下午五点，我们精疲力竭，简直累得不行。

610
00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.210
We thought, here's what we're going to do.
我们想，我们打算这么做。

611
00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:36.170
We're going to go into a little pub.
我们要去一家小酒馆。

612
00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:38.270
We're going to get a bite to eat.
我们要吃点东西。

613
00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:39.850
We're going to have a drink.
我们要喝上一杯。

614
00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:46.770
We're going to force ourselves to stay awake until 7 p.m., and then we're going to go back to the hotel and fall asleep.
我们要强迫自己撑到晚上七点，然后回酒店睡觉。

615
00:22:46.990 --> 00:22:47.130
Right.
对。

616
00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:47.870
That was your plan.
这就是你们的计划。

617
00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:50.630
Go to the pub, power through, and then go to bed.
去酒馆，撑过去，然后去睡觉。

618
00:22:50.850 --> 00:22:51.250
Correct.
没错。

619
00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:59.310
We get to the pub, we order our drink, and we see a sign that says, Poker Tournament, starting at 6 p.m.
我们到了酒馆，点了酒，然后看到一个牌子写着：扑克锦标赛，下午六点开始。

620
00:22:59.450 --> 00:22:59.870
All right.
好吧。

621
00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:01.130
I have to interject here.
我得插一句。

622
00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:06.630
So, my BFF, Jenna Fisher, is a flippin' fantastic poker player.
我的闺蜜珍娜·费舍尔，是个超级厉害的扑克玩家。

623
00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:09.010
I don't know if I'm fantastic, but I love playing.
我不知道自己算不算厉害，但我很喜欢玩。

624
00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:09.470
Okay.
好吧。

625
00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:10.690
No, you're fantastic.
不，你真的很厉害。

626
00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:16.870
And I once went with her to the Celebrity Poker Showdown story for later, but she's really good at poker.
我曾经陪她去参加过《名人扑克对决》，那是后话了，但她扑克真的打得很好。

627
00:23:17.050 --> 00:23:18.170
I came in second place.
我拿了第二名。

628
00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:19.290
You came in, I mean, that's a-
你拿了，我是说，那可是——

629
00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.290
Behind Keegan Michael Key.
输给了基根-迈克尔·凯。

630
00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.010
He won.
他赢了。

631
00:23:21.190 --> 00:23:25.850
That's a big flex, because you beat Michael Ian Black, who still tells me that you beat him in poker.
那可是很了不起的成就，因为你赢了迈克尔·伊恩·布莱克，他到现在还跟我念叨你赢过他。

632
00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.870
And, I mean, you guys, I-
而且，我是说，各位，我——

633
00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.250
I also just want to say, all of this is before I had children.
我还想说，这一切都是在我有孩子之前的事了。

634
00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:30.650
Yeah.
是啊。

635
00:23:30.790 --> 00:23:32.010
I barely play poker anymore.
我现在几乎不怎么玩扑克了。

636
00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:33.650
I can't stay awake for anything.
我什么都撑不住，没法熬夜。

637
00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:35.670
I know, but you are really good.
我知道，但你真的很厉害。

638
00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.250
Back in your day, lady.
那是你当年的风采，女士。

639
00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:38.190
Back in the day.
往日时光。

640
00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.490
Back in your day before kids.
在你还没孩子的时候。

641
00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:39.850
In my youth.
在我年轻的时候。

642
00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:40.690
In your youth.
在你年轻的时候。

643
00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:42.170
You were quite the poker player.
你曾经是个很厉害的扑克玩家。

644
00:23:42.570 --> 00:23:46.950
I think I can win poker with, like, two pairs of threes, and I have all the bravado.
我觉得我能靠两对三赢下扑克，而且我气势十足。

645
00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:47.930
Two pairs of threes.
两对三。

646
00:23:47.930 --> 00:23:49.110
That would be four of a kind.
那可是四条啊。

647
00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:50.350
You can.
你可以的。

648
00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:50.790
Okay.
好吧。

649
00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:52.310
You can win poker with that, Angela.
安吉拉，你确实能靠那个赢下扑克。

650
00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:52.670
Okay.
好吧。

651
00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:54.110
So, see, this is the problem.
你看，这就是问题所在。

652
00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:56.370
But I have no idea what I'm doing.
但我根本不知道自己在做什么。

653
00:23:56.530 --> 00:24:00.490
And I think sometimes I mess up a table just because I have such confidence and I have nothing.
我觉得有时候我把牌局搞砸，纯粹是因为我表现得太自信，其实肚子里根本没货。

654
00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:01.910
And then people are like, argh.
然后大家就会觉得，啊，真无语。

655
00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:02.350
Okay.
好吧。

656
00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:03.850
Sometimes that's the best strategy.
有时候这反而是最好的策略。

657
00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:04.490
Okay, go.
好，开始吧。

658
00:24:04.650 --> 00:24:05.550
You're in Scotland.
你们当时在苏格兰。

659
00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:06.290
We're in Scotland.
我们在苏格兰。

660
00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:07.430
You're trying to stay awake.
你们想让自己保持清醒。

661
00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:07.850
So tired.
太累了。

662
00:24:08.110 --> 00:24:09.710
We sign up for the poker tournament.
我们报名参加了扑克锦标赛。

663
00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:12.310
Lee, my husband, he plays poker as well.
我丈夫李也打扑克。

664
00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:14.510
We're thinking, here's what we'll do.
我们心想，我们就这么办。

665
00:24:14.650 --> 00:24:17.010
We'll join the poker tournament at 6 p.m.
下午六点参加锦标赛。

666
00:24:17.570 --> 00:24:18.670
We'll be done at 7.
七点就能结束。

667
00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:20.730
And this is how we're going to stay awake that extra hour.
这样我们就能多撑一个小时不睡觉。

668
00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:22.950
You're going to play an hour of poker, and then you're going to go to bed.
你们打算打一个小时扑克，然后就去睡觉。

669
00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:23.410
Go to bed.
去睡觉。

670
00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:25.250
We enter the tournament.
我们参加了比赛。

671
00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:26.950
We start playing.
开始打牌。

672
00:24:27.630 --> 00:24:28.550
We start winning.
开始赢牌。

673
00:24:28.830 --> 00:24:33.290
You're like the two Americans who came in, and now you're kicking butt in this pub in Scotland.
你们就像两个突然闯入的美国人，在苏格兰的一家酒吧里大杀四方。

674
00:24:33.630 --> 00:24:38.310
So much so that we make it to the final table.
我们甚至一路打进了决赛桌。

675
00:24:38.550 --> 00:24:39.410
What time is this?
那时候几点了？

676
00:24:39.430 --> 00:24:40.470
How long have you been there now?
你们已经在那里待了多久了？

677
00:24:40.490 --> 00:24:41.330
It is now midnight.
当时已经是午夜了。

678
00:24:41.470 --> 00:24:41.990
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

679
00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:45.630
We are out of our minds.
我们当时神志不清。

680
00:24:46.230 --> 00:24:46.590
Exhausted.
精疲力竭。

681
00:24:46.630 --> 00:24:48.050
I don't even know what I'm doing.
我甚至不知道自己在干什么。

682
00:24:48.050 --> 00:24:50.050
It's probably why I was doing so well.
可能正因如此我才打得那么好。

683
00:24:50.130 --> 00:24:50.930
Because you're so loopy.
因为你当时晕乎乎的。

684
00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:52.270
You're playing the best poker of your life.
你打出了人生中最高水平的扑克。

685
00:24:52.450 --> 00:24:57.070
Lee and I are both at the final table, and we keep checking in with each other, saying,
我和李都进了决赛桌，我们不停地互相确认，问对方，

686
00:24:57.210 --> 00:24:57.870
like, should we quit?
比如，我们要不要退出？

687
00:24:57.950 --> 00:25:00.790
A couple times, Lee went all in, because he's like, I'm so tired.
有几次，李直接全押了，因为他觉得，我太累了。

688
00:25:00.870 --> 00:25:01.430
Just all in.
就是直接全押。

689
00:25:01.490 --> 00:25:02.330
And he would win.
结果他还赢了。

690
00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:05.490
Finally, I get down to the final two.
最后，我进入了单挑环节。

691
00:25:05.850 --> 00:25:07.070
It's 2 a.m.
当时是凌晨两点。

692
00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:09.210
And it's you and one other person?
剩下你和另外一个人？

693
00:25:09.470 --> 00:25:15.610
One local Scottish guy who played every week in the tournament.
一个每周都来参加比赛的当地苏格兰人。

694
00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:16.770
And here you are.
而你就在那里。

695
00:25:16.850 --> 00:25:19.790
This American on her vacation.
一个来度假的美国人。

696
00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:22.630
And I won.
然后我赢了。

697
00:25:22.870 --> 00:25:24.310
You won the whole thing.
你赢了整场比赛。

698
00:25:24.350 --> 00:25:25.030
I won.
我赢了。

699
00:25:25.170 --> 00:25:26.450
I won the whole thing.
我赢了整场比赛。

700
00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:28.370
I won 200 pounds.
我赢了200英镑。

701
00:25:28.790 --> 00:25:29.270
Wow.
哇。

702
00:25:29.870 --> 00:25:30.350
Amazing.
太棒了。

703
00:25:31.530 --> 00:25:33.330
Lee and I couldn't believe it.
我和李简直不敢相信。

704
00:25:33.490 --> 00:25:35.570
Everyone in the pub was a little bit like, yay.
酒吧里的每个人都有点，耶。

705
00:25:36.390 --> 00:25:37.330
Yay for her.
为她欢呼。

706
00:25:37.550 --> 00:25:39.570
Did you get your name, like, up on the wall or something?
你的名字被写在墙上之类的了吗？

707
00:25:39.570 --> 00:25:44.030
I got my name up on the leaderboard, and I was supposed to come back for the championship
我的名字上了排行榜，我本该回去参加几个月后举行的

708
00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:48.150
table that was happening in several months.
冠军赛的。

709
00:25:48.150 --> 00:25:50.390
Of course, we all knew I wasn't going to show up.
当然，我们都知道我不会去。

710
00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:53.210
So I think the runner-up guy got to take my place.
所以我猜是那个亚军顶替了我的位置。

711
00:25:53.570 --> 00:25:58.830
And then we went back to the hotel, and we slept so well, and I suffered no jet lag for
然后我们回到酒店，睡得特别香，那次旅行剩下的时间里

712
00:25:58.830 --> 00:25:59.830
the rest of that trip.
我一点时差反应都没有。

713
00:25:59.990 --> 00:26:00.910
So this was your story?
所以这就是你的故事？

714
00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:03.190
This was the story in the United magazine.
这就是《联合》杂志上的那个故事。

715
00:26:04.070 --> 00:26:07.210
And I was so proud to be in that magazine.
我为能上那本杂志感到无比自豪。

716
00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:08.070
I'm with Michael Scott.
我和迈克尔·斯科特同感。

717
00:26:08.070 --> 00:26:09.590
That would have been a heck of a read.
那读起来一定很带劲。

718
00:26:10.430 --> 00:26:11.450
I got copies.
我留了些副本。

719
00:26:11.610 --> 00:26:12.730
I sent them to my mom.
我寄给我妈了。

720
00:26:12.890 --> 00:26:14.170
I sent them to my in-laws.
我寄给我岳父母了。

721
00:26:14.190 --> 00:26:15.330
I have one at home.
我家里也留了一本。

722
00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:19.350
I want you guys to know, I woke up back here in the U.S.
我想让你们知道，我在美国醒来时，

723
00:26:19.390 --> 00:26:21.470
of A., and I had a text from my
收到了我苏格兰最好的朋友发来的短信，

724
00:26:21.470 --> 00:26:25.750
best friend in Scotland, and there was a photo of her in a pub.
照片里她正在一家酒吧里。

725
00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:28.050
Wearing my hat that I had bought, by the way.
顺便说一下，戴着我买的那顶帽子。

726
00:26:28.270 --> 00:26:29.030
Wearing your hat that you bought.
戴着你买的那顶帽子。

727
00:26:29.030 --> 00:26:29.690
My wool hat.
我的羊毛帽。

728
00:26:29.830 --> 00:26:30.830
And, like, smiling.
而且，还在笑。

729
00:26:31.090 --> 00:26:32.610
And I was like, what is going on?
我当时就想，这到底是怎么回事？

730
00:26:32.650 --> 00:26:34.350
And you were like, I won a poker tournament.
然后你说，我赢了一场扑克锦标赛。

731
00:26:34.350 --> 00:26:36.090
I was like, you're supposed to be sleeping.
我说，你不是应该在睡觉吗？

732
00:26:36.690 --> 00:26:37.010
Yeah.
是啊。

733
00:26:37.010 --> 00:26:37.060
Yeah.
是啊。

734
00:26:37.430 --> 00:26:40.890
But that's, I mean, truly, that is, like, maybe one of my proudest moments.
但说真的，那可能是我最引以为傲的时刻之一。

735
00:26:41.030 --> 00:26:42.890
Yeah, that's a pretty rock star moment, lady.
没错，那真是个摇滚巨星般的时刻，女士。

736
00:26:43.110 --> 00:26:43.570
Thank you.
谢谢。

737
00:26:43.750 --> 00:26:45.330
Well, we should probably get back to the episode.
好吧，我们大概该回到剧集了。

738
00:26:45.630 --> 00:26:48.670
This is the cringiest episode of The Office so far.
这是《办公室》目前为止最让人尴尬的一集。

739
00:26:49.830 --> 00:26:50.650
Not ever.
不是史上最尴尬。

740
00:26:50.910 --> 00:26:54.650
I mean, Scott's Tots, but it's cringey.
我是说，《斯科特的托特们》那集，但这一集也很尴尬。

741
00:26:54.850 --> 00:26:56.730
But Diversity Day is pretty cringey, too.
不过《多元化日》那集也挺尴尬的。

742
00:26:56.950 --> 00:27:01.690
But the whole scene where Michael is talking to Katie about coffee, I was dying.
但迈克尔和凯蒂谈论咖啡的那整场戏，我简直要笑死了。

743
00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:02.290
Oh, I was dying.
噢，我快笑死了。

744
00:27:02.290 --> 00:27:06.230
What I was also got so weirded out when he was like, you know, all I'm trying to do here
还有当他说，你知道，我在这里所做的一切

745
00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:07.390
is just break down walls.
只是为了打破隔阂。

746
00:27:07.630 --> 00:27:09.270
I just try to break down walls.
我只是试图打破隔阂。

747
00:27:09.670 --> 00:27:12.110
I was like, what is he talking about?
我当时就想，他在说什么啊？

748
00:27:12.290 --> 00:27:12.770
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

749
00:27:12.790 --> 00:27:14.910
And she plays it so well.
而且她演得太好了。

750
00:27:15.030 --> 00:27:15.690
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

751
00:27:16.230 --> 00:27:19.790
And then that scene with Brian over my shoulder asking me if I'm jealous.
还有布莱恩在我身后问我是否嫉妒的那场戏。

752
00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:22.710
I laughed so hard during that scene.
那场戏我笑得好厉害。

753
00:27:22.970 --> 00:27:27.290
What was difficult was that I was supposed to sit there and be doing my work.
难点在于我本该坐在那儿专心工作。

754
00:27:27.290 --> 00:27:31.630
And he is hovering over me and then insulting me.
而他却在我身后徘徊，还羞辱我。

755
00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:32.830
And I could not get through it.
我根本演不下去。

756
00:27:32.990 --> 00:27:36.490
Every time he would start his sentence, it would make me laugh.
每次他一开口，我就忍不住笑场。

757
00:27:36.730 --> 00:27:40.790
That was a scene that I probably laughed the most in when I was shooting this episode.
那可能是我拍这一集时笑得最多的一场戏了。

758
00:27:41.210 --> 00:27:43.550
And this leads me into a fan question from Delaney.
这让我想到了粉丝Delaney的一个问题。

759
00:27:43.850 --> 00:27:46.470
Did you guys ever get offended by the scripts personally?
你们有没有因为剧本内容而感到被冒犯过？

760
00:27:46.570 --> 00:27:50.050
Like in this episode, how Pam is compared to Katie the whole time?
比如在这一集中，帕姆一直被拿来和凯蒂作比较？

761
00:27:50.190 --> 00:27:51.590
Jenna, did you take that personally?
珍娜，你当时介意吗？

762
00:27:52.270 --> 00:27:53.150
I didn't.
我不介意。

763
00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:58.050
Well, I didn't either because I felt like a lot of our comedy was it was a little bit
嗯，我也不介意，因为我觉得我们的喜剧风格多少有点

764
00:27:58.050 --> 00:27:58.750
of a free for all.
随心所欲。

765
00:27:58.870 --> 00:28:02.950
Like everyone was going to have a moment, you know, where they were sort of the butt of the
就像每个人都会有那么一刻，你知道，成为大家

766
00:28:02.950 --> 00:28:04.750
joke, but it was never malicious.
取笑的对象，但那绝非恶意。

767
00:28:04.750 --> 00:28:06.950
It was just it served the script.
那只是为了服务剧本。

768
00:28:07.130 --> 00:28:07.930
It served the story.
为了服务剧情。

769
00:28:08.150 --> 00:28:09.070
I never took offense.
我从未感到被冒犯。

770
00:28:09.310 --> 00:28:15.890
Also, I feel like so much of comedy and comedians is self-deprecating in nature.
而且我觉得喜剧和喜剧演员很大程度上本质上都是自嘲的。

771
00:28:16.110 --> 00:28:16.290
Yeah.
没错。

772
00:28:16.450 --> 00:28:19.710
And so we're a group of people who are pretty honest with ourselves.
所以我们这群人对自己都挺坦诚的。

773
00:28:19.930 --> 00:28:20.510
Don't you think?
你不觉得吗？

774
00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:20.830
Yeah.
是啊。

775
00:28:20.990 --> 00:28:22.310
It wasn't offensive to me.
我并不觉得被冒犯。

776
00:28:22.310 --> 00:28:28.590
It was also it was the idea that has happened to all of us where a more attractive person
而且这其实是我们每个人都经历过的情况，当一个更有魅力的人

777
00:28:28.590 --> 00:28:33.590
walks in the room and is getting all the attention and then you feel you feel jealous.
走进房间，吸引了所有人的注意，你就会感到嫉妒。

778
00:28:33.670 --> 00:28:35.650
But I enjoyed this episode.
但我很喜欢这一集。

779
00:28:35.790 --> 00:28:37.570
I loved playing with all those feelings.
我很享受演绎这些复杂的情绪。

780
00:28:37.730 --> 00:28:40.270
I was going to say it was a lot of human moments for Pam.
我正想说，这对帕姆来说有很多展现人性的时刻。

781
00:28:40.410 --> 00:28:43.750
Just seeing how Jim was affected and how that affected her.
看着吉姆受到的影响，以及这又如何影响了她。

782
00:28:44.030 --> 00:28:45.350
And it was fantastic.
这太棒了。

783
00:28:45.350 --> 00:28:46.890
I thought you did an excellent job.
我觉得你演得非常出色。

784
00:28:46.890 --> 00:28:48.390
I have on one of my note cards.
我的卡片上写着呢。

785
00:28:48.670 --> 00:28:49.730
Where is it, Jenna?
在哪儿呢，珍娜？

786
00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:51.150
What does it say?
上面写了什么？

787
00:28:51.650 --> 00:28:52.110
Jenna.
珍娜。

788
00:28:52.310 --> 00:28:52.970
That was brilliant.
那段表演太精彩了。

789
00:28:53.310 --> 00:28:54.030
She was.
她演得真好。

790
00:28:54.250 --> 00:28:55.010
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

791
00:28:55.050 --> 00:28:56.030
You were so good.
你演得太棒了。

792
00:28:56.190 --> 00:28:59.830
Oh, I don't want to like get us off your I know you have your list, lady.
噢，我不想打断你，我知道你还有你的清单要念，女士。

793
00:29:00.110 --> 00:29:03.250
But the moment when she's like, what are you going to do?
但当她说“你打算怎么办”的那一刻，

794
00:29:03.350 --> 00:29:05.570
And he's like, oh, I think actually I'm going to see Katie.
而他说“噢，我想我其实打算去见凯蒂”。

795
00:29:05.570 --> 00:29:08.010
The look on your face as Pam.
你作为帕姆时的表情。

796
00:29:08.270 --> 00:29:11.390
What you did with your eyes in that moment was so amazing.
那一刻你眼神的处理简直太绝了。

797
00:29:11.730 --> 00:29:12.490
It's interesting.
真有意思。

