00:41:01.330 --> 00:41:07.170
So to see him sort of humble himself like that to Katie and get humiliated, I just felt
所以看到他那样在凯蒂面前放低姿态却遭到羞辱，我当时觉得

1124
00:41:07.170 --> 00:41:09.970
like I didn't even want him to think that I had witnessed it.
我甚至不想让他觉得我目睹了这一切。

1125
00:41:10.190 --> 00:41:11.230
I didn't see it.
我没看见。

1126
00:41:11.330 --> 00:41:12.050
It didn't happen.
什么都没发生。

1127
00:41:12.210 --> 00:41:12.610
It's okay.
没关系的。

1128
00:41:12.910 --> 00:41:14.730
That's, I think, what she was thinking.
我想，这就是她当时的想法。

1129
00:41:14.910 --> 00:41:16.390
And that's why I didn't look up.
这就是我为什么没有抬头看。

1130
00:41:16.490 --> 00:41:18.610
I was literally trying to be invisible in the moment.
那一刻我真的在努力让自己隐形。

1131
00:41:18.610 --> 00:41:24.170
Well, after that, you have a line that is one of my favorite lines of your character where
好吧，在那之后，你有一句台词是我最喜欢的你这个角色的台词，

1132
00:41:24.170 --> 00:41:25.670
you describe your favorite colors.
你描述了你最喜欢的颜色。

1133
00:41:26.410 --> 00:41:28.070
This is a fan question from Emmy.
这是一个来自艾米的粉丝提问。

1134
00:41:28.250 --> 00:41:32.070
Angela, did you improvise the scene where you discuss your colors being different shades
安吉拉，你讨论自己喜欢的颜色是不同深浅的灰色那场戏，是即兴发挥的吗？

1135
00:41:32.070 --> 00:41:32.530
of gray?
是的，是我即兴发挥的。

1136
00:41:32.790 --> 00:41:33.510
Yes, I did.
我就知道。

1137
00:41:33.630 --> 00:41:34.470
I knew it.
是的，是我即兴发挥的。

1138
00:41:34.610 --> 00:41:35.190
Yes, I did.
是的，是我即兴发挥的。

1139
00:41:35.350 --> 00:41:40.870
In the episode, Dwight is looking in at the conference room at Katie and Angela sort of
在那一集中，德怀特正往会议室里看，看着凯蒂和安吉拉在

1140
00:41:40.870 --> 00:41:43.170
talking, and we didn't have any scripted dialogue.
交谈，我们当时没有任何剧本台词。

1141
00:41:43.350 --> 00:41:44.930
So they said, can you just kind of banter?
所以他们说，你们能随便聊聊吗？

1142
00:41:45.130 --> 00:41:47.850
And I didn't even know if it would make it in, you know?
我当时甚至不知道这段会不会被剪进去，你知道吗？

1143
00:41:47.850 --> 00:41:50.170
And so that scene was improvised.
所以那场戏是即兴表演的。

1144
00:41:50.390 --> 00:41:54.490
And it starts off with Amy as Katie saying, well, you seem to like to touch things.
开始是艾米饰演的凯蒂说，嗯，你看起来喜欢触摸东西。

1145
00:41:54.950 --> 00:41:59.030
And then I just responded, I don't like to necessarily touch things.
然后我回应说，我不一定喜欢触摸东西。

1146
00:41:59.030 --> 00:42:00.290
I'm shopping, you know?
我是在购物，你知道吗？

1147
00:42:00.430 --> 00:42:01.250
I loved that line.
我太喜欢那句台词了。

1148
00:42:01.410 --> 00:42:03.090
And then she said, well, what color do you like?
然后她说，好吧，那你喜欢什么颜色？

1149
00:42:03.130 --> 00:42:04.130
And this was all improvised.
这些全都是即兴发挥的。

1150
00:42:04.250 --> 00:42:07.110
And I said, gray, dark gray, charcoal.
我说，灰色，深灰色，炭灰色。

1151
00:42:07.810 --> 00:42:10.470
And it made it in, and that was really fun.
它最终被采用了，真的很有趣。

1152
00:42:10.670 --> 00:42:13.690
And then that line ended up in an article in the newspaper.
后来那句台词还出现在了一篇报纸文章里。

1153
00:42:13.690 --> 00:42:16.350
It was talking about what sums up the show.
文章里在讨论什么能概括这部剧。

1154
00:42:16.350 --> 00:42:21.810
And they said, well, the character Angela's line, gray, dark gray, charcoal, really sets
他们说，安吉拉那个关于灰色、深灰、炭灰的台词，真的奠定了

1155
00:42:21.810 --> 00:42:22.390
the tone.
整部剧的基调。

1156
00:42:22.390 --> 00:42:24.130
And I was so proud of that.
我对此感到非常自豪。

1157
00:42:24.490 --> 00:42:28.390
It really then informed a lot of your wardrobe after that.
那之后，它确实影响了你大部分的服装选择。

1158
00:42:28.590 --> 00:42:33.450
You had been kind of wearing these muted colors, but that became your uniform moving forward.
你之前一直穿这些柔和的颜色，但那之后它就成了你的标配。

1159
00:42:33.770 --> 00:42:35.170
Okay, Jenna, what else do you have?
好了，珍娜，你还有什么？

1160
00:42:35.290 --> 00:42:35.650
All right.
好的。

1161
00:42:35.870 --> 00:42:38.550
The scene where Ryan and Michael are cleaning out his car.
瑞安和迈克尔清理他车子的那场戏。

1162
00:42:39.430 --> 00:42:41.070
That was not improvised.
那不是即兴表演。

1163
00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:42.170
No, that was scripted.
不，那是写在剧本里的。

1164
00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:43.430
A lot of people asked.
很多人都问过。

1165
00:42:43.670 --> 00:42:44.330
All of it.
全都是。

1166
00:42:44.490 --> 00:42:45.290
Blue blaSt.
蓝色冲击。

1167
00:42:45.810 --> 00:42:46.570
Smell alike.
闻起来一样。

1168
00:42:46.930 --> 00:42:48.550
How many filet of fish do you eat?
你到底吃了多少个麦香鱼？

1169
00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:50.110
All of those lines are in the script.
所有这些台词都在剧本里。

1170
00:42:50.330 --> 00:42:51.110
I checked.
我确认过了。

1171
00:42:51.530 --> 00:42:55.870
Because when I was watching it, it was so hard for me to believe that it was not improvised
因为我在看的时候，实在很难相信那不是即兴发挥的，

1172
00:42:55.870 --> 00:42:58.010
that I went back to my script and I read it.
所以我回去翻了剧本，读了一遍。

1173
00:42:58.130 --> 00:43:02.970
And I think that it just points to how good the writing was on our show.
我觉得这正好说明了我们剧的剧本有多棒。

1174
00:43:03.310 --> 00:43:03.490
Fantastic.
太棒了。

1175
00:43:03.490 --> 00:43:04.810
Just how good.
就是那么棒。

1176
00:43:04.950 --> 00:43:07.430
And also how good the actors were.
还有演员们也演得非常好。

1177
00:43:08.030 --> 00:43:13.610
I mean, BJ and Steve in that scene, just absolutely brilliant.
我是说，BJ和史蒂夫在那场戏里的表现，简直太精彩了。

1178
00:43:14.050 --> 00:43:19.310
Mindy also told me that the reference to the filet of fishes is a nod to her disgusting
明迪也告诉我，关于麦香鱼的那个梗，其实是致敬她现实生活中对

1179
00:43:19.310 --> 00:43:20.930
love of filet of fish in real life.
麦香鱼那种令人作呕的喜爱。

1180
00:43:20.990 --> 00:43:22.770
Or just her love for McDonald's.
或者说仅仅是她对麦当劳的喜爱。

1181
00:43:22.890 --> 00:43:24.510
She loves McDonald's.
她很爱麦当劳。

1182
00:43:25.530 --> 00:43:28.310
But that she really does love a filet of fish.
但她是真的非常喜欢麦香鱼。

1183
00:43:28.310 --> 00:43:34.590
I loved in this scene, too, when Michael's like, that was over a period of time, okay?
我也很喜欢这场戏里迈克尔说的那句：那是一段时间内吃的，好吗？

1184
00:43:34.590 --> 00:43:35.350
It was over a month.
那是过了一个月。

1185
00:43:35.470 --> 00:43:36.130
It was over a month.
那是过了一个月。

1186
00:43:36.510 --> 00:43:38.290
And Ryan the temp goes, still.
然后临时工瑞安说：那也一样。

1187
00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:38.910
Yeah.
没错。

1188
00:43:40.010 --> 00:43:42.070
I could watch that scene over and over again.
那场戏我可以看上一遍又一遍。

1189
00:43:42.190 --> 00:43:43.030
I think that's a gem.
我觉得那是个精品。

1190
00:43:43.550 --> 00:43:47.470
I think if you haven't rewatched this episode, but you're listening to the podcast, just please
我想如果你还没重温过这一集，但正在听我们的播客，请务必

1191
00:43:47.470 --> 00:43:48.470
go watch that scene.
去看看那场戏。

1192
00:43:48.610 --> 00:43:49.190
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

1193
00:43:49.810 --> 00:43:50.770
Blue is not a flavor.
蓝色不是一种口味。

1194
00:43:51.890 --> 00:43:52.890
I have a note card.
我有一张笔记卡。

1195
00:43:53.110 --> 00:43:53.690
Say it.
说吧。

1196
00:43:53.690 --> 00:43:59.510
Okay, this is a great, great Dwight line when he says, shroots produce very thirsty babies.
好的，这是德怀特一句非常非常棒的台词，他说：施鲁特家族的孩子生来就很渴。

1197
00:43:59.810 --> 00:44:00.610
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

1198
00:44:00.810 --> 00:44:01.870
That's a famous line.
那是一句名台词。

1199
00:44:01.970 --> 00:44:02.870
That's a famous line.
那是一句名台词。

1200
00:44:02.990 --> 00:44:06.110
And when I was pregnant, I was pregnant season five of The Office.
我怀孕的时候，正好是拍《办公室》第五季期间。

1201
00:44:06.210 --> 00:44:11.710
And I got a gift of a t-shirt that said, shroots produce very thirsty babies.
我还收到了一件T恤作为礼物，上面写着“甜菜根会让宝宝变得非常口渴”。

1202
00:44:11.730 --> 00:44:13.170
And it was a maternity shirt.
那是一件孕妇装。

1203
00:44:13.370 --> 00:44:14.130
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1204
00:44:14.250 --> 00:44:18.270
And I wore that around my big belly and people would freak out.
我挺着大肚子穿那件衣服，人们都会被吓一跳。

1205
00:44:18.290 --> 00:44:19.330
I still have it.
我至今还留着它。

1206
00:44:19.430 --> 00:44:20.110
I still have it.
我至今还留着它。

1207
00:44:20.210 --> 00:44:22.330
Oh, do you have a picture of yourself in that?
噢，你有穿那件衣服的照片吗？

1208
00:44:22.330 --> 00:44:23.330
I will look.
我找找看。

1209
00:44:23.410 --> 00:44:25.930
But if I don't, I'll just take a picture of myself in it.
如果找不到，我就再穿上它拍一张。

1210
00:44:26.010 --> 00:44:29.250
And I'll have to post that on Office Ladies Pod because I still have that shirt.
我得把它发到《办公室女士》播客上，因为我确实还留着那件衣服。

1211
00:44:29.450 --> 00:44:29.850
You should.
你应该发。

1212
00:44:30.010 --> 00:44:30.210
Definitely.
绝对应该。

1213
00:44:30.610 --> 00:44:33.190
Here is something that everybody wrote in about.
这是大家写信问得最多的一个问题。

1214
00:44:33.310 --> 00:44:35.070
This was one of our most popular questions.
这是我们最热门的问题之一。

1215
00:44:35.810 --> 00:44:39.330
What's up with the wrong parking lot at the end of this episode?
为什么这集结尾的停车场不对劲？

1216
00:44:39.550 --> 00:44:43.250
That's because this was the original set before we moved.
那是因为在我们搬迁之前，那是最初的片场。

1217
00:44:43.390 --> 00:44:47.550
The first six episodes, we all filmed at an actual office building in Culver City.
前六集我们都是在卡尔弗城的一栋真实办公楼里拍摄的。

1218
00:44:47.710 --> 00:44:48.770
And that was the parking lot.
那就是当时的停车场。

1219
00:44:48.950 --> 00:44:49.270
Yes.
没错。

1220
00:44:49.270 --> 00:44:53.350
So when we moved in season two and beyond, we had two soundstages.
所以当我们第二季及以后搬走时，我们有了两个摄影棚。

1221
00:44:53.510 --> 00:44:59.970
One soundstage was a recreation of the office, that interior office that we shot in the first year.
一个摄影棚是第一年拍摄时那个办公室内部的复刻版。

1222
00:45:00.390 --> 00:45:02.930
The other building is where the writers worked.
另一栋楼是编剧们工作的地方。

1223
00:45:03.050 --> 00:45:04.270
And it was just an office building.
那只是一栋普通的办公楼。

1224
00:45:04.270 --> 00:45:06.330
And that was just the parking lot for it.
那也只是那栋楼的停车场。

1225
00:45:06.470 --> 00:45:06.850
Yes.
是的。

1226
00:45:07.030 --> 00:45:10.390
And that is where we filmed the Dunder Mifflin parking lot.
那就是我们拍摄邓德·米弗林停车场的地方。

1227
00:45:10.390 --> 00:45:15.650
So it was really interesting because we had our warehouse set over there.
所以这很有趣，因为我们的仓库布景在那边。

1228
00:45:15.990 --> 00:45:17.770
And then we had the parking lot.
然后我们有停车场。

1229
00:45:17.950 --> 00:45:20.470
And we had the lobby and the elevator where Hank's at.
还有大堂和汉克所在的电梯。

1230
00:45:20.670 --> 00:45:20.990
Yes.
没错。

1231
00:45:21.150 --> 00:45:22.430
All of that was one building.
所有这些都在同一栋楼里。

1232
00:45:22.430 --> 00:45:24.750
But then the Dunder Mifflin building was something else.
但邓德·米弗林的办公楼是另一回事。

1233
00:45:24.790 --> 00:45:28.810
So if we had to do a scene where you see us walk out,
所以如果我们必须拍一场大家走出来的戏，

1234
00:45:28.850 --> 00:45:36.670
we would have to start that scene in one building and then move all the cameras and all of us over to the other building and then get the exterior version of it.
我们就得先在一栋楼里开始拍摄，然后把所有摄像机和所有人都搬到另一栋楼，再去拍外景部分。

1235
00:45:36.810 --> 00:45:37.210
Yes.
是的。

1236
00:45:37.210 --> 00:45:38.230
It was quite complicated.
这相当复杂。

1237
00:45:38.450 --> 00:45:38.770
It was.
确实如此。

1238
00:45:39.750 --> 00:45:44.870
Basically, when we filmed in one stage indoors, we filmed another stage outdoors for the most part.
基本上，当我们在一个摄影棚拍室内戏时，大部分时间我们都在另一个摄影棚拍室外戏。

1239
00:45:45.030 --> 00:45:51.170
But that parking lot is not the Dunder Mifflin parking lot that you see from season two and beyond.
但那个停车场并不是你在第二季及以后看到的那个邓德·米弗林停车场。

1240
00:45:51.410 --> 00:45:53.390
And I have a story about that parking lot.
关于那个停车场，我有个故事。

1241
00:45:53.610 --> 00:45:59.870
You see in that final shot, it starts with Michael and Jim and Katie leaving.
你看最后一个镜头，开始是迈克尔、吉姆和凯蒂离开。

1242
00:46:00.290 --> 00:46:01.310
She's got her big bag.
她提着个大包。

1243
00:46:01.570 --> 00:46:05.650
Michael realizes that Jim is going to be giving her a ride home because they're going to get drinks.
迈克尔意识到吉姆要送她回家，因为他们要去喝一杯。

1244
00:46:05.650 --> 00:46:13.630
And then it reveals Pam and Roy backing up in Roy's truck and Pam clocks Jim and Katie.
然后镜头切到帕姆和罗伊倒车，罗伊开着卡车，帕姆注意到了吉姆和凯蒂。

1245
00:46:14.670 --> 00:46:23.030
So David and I had to sit in that truck in the parking lot and wait a very long time until everyone came out and did that scene.
所以大卫和我必须坐在停车场的那辆卡车里，等了很长时间，直到所有人都出来拍那场戏。

1246
00:46:23.030 --> 00:46:26.250
And we had a little walkie talkie inside the truck and they would say, go.
我们在卡车里有个小对讲机，他们会说“开始”。

1247
00:46:26.630 --> 00:46:32.690
And then David would back up and we would pull out and the camera would get that shot of me looking sad and we would drive off.
然后大卫就会倒车，我们开出去，摄像机拍下我看起来很伤心的镜头，然后我们就开车离开。

1248
00:46:32.830 --> 00:46:33.830
And then they would say, reset.
接着他们会说“重置”。

1249
00:46:34.190 --> 00:46:37.450
And we would bring the truck back and then we would wait a very long time.
我们就把卡车开回来，然后又要等很长时间。

1250
00:46:38.210 --> 00:46:46.850
At the end of the night, they reset us back into the parking lot and we sat there and we sat there in the truck.
那天晚上结束时，他们让我们回到停车场重置，我们就坐在卡车里一直等着。

1251
00:46:47.150 --> 00:46:48.410
We sat there in the truck.
我们当时坐在卡车里。

1252
00:46:48.570 --> 00:46:53.830
And then all of a sudden, we saw everyone driving away in their own cars.
突然之间，我们看到大家都开着自己的车离开了。

1253
00:46:54.150 --> 00:46:54.750
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1254
00:46:55.170 --> 00:46:56.990
They left us in the truck.
他们把我们留在卡车里了。

1255
00:46:57.170 --> 00:46:59.570
They forgot to tell us that they had wrapped.
他们忘了告诉我们他们已经收工了。

1256
00:46:59.990 --> 00:47:00.730
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

1257
00:47:00.730 --> 00:47:01.290
For the day.
当天的拍摄结束了。

1258
00:47:01.550 --> 00:47:03.310
And we were all done and we were leaving.
我们都拍完了，正准备离开。

1259
00:47:03.490 --> 00:47:04.170
You were done.
你们拍完了。

1260
00:47:04.170 --> 00:47:05.890
You were changing clothes.
你们在换衣服。

1261
00:47:06.110 --> 00:47:07.750
You were getting in your cars.
你们在坐进各自的车里。

1262
00:47:07.750 --> 00:47:09.430
We saw the director leave.
我们看到导演离开了。

1263
00:47:09.690 --> 00:47:10.650
We saw actors.
我们看到演员们也走了。

1264
00:47:10.950 --> 00:47:13.130
David and I were like, what?
大卫和我当时心想，怎么回事？

1265
00:47:13.410 --> 00:47:13.930
What?
什么？

1266
00:47:13.930 --> 00:47:14.930
What is going on?
到底发生了什么？

1267
00:47:15.750 --> 00:47:17.610
So, and here's the thing.
所以，重点是这样的。

1268
00:47:17.770 --> 00:47:19.190
I've talked about this before.
我之前提到过这件事。

1269
00:47:19.450 --> 00:47:22.190
David Denman and I were very good friends in real life.
大卫·丹曼和我在现实生活中是非常好的朋友。

1270
00:47:22.350 --> 00:47:29.970
We talked about in the basketball episode how you and I became best friends because we had to sit on that bench for hours and hours.
我们在聊篮球那一集时说过，你和我之所以成为最好的朋友，是因为我们不得不在那条长凳上坐上好几个小时。

1271
00:47:30.630 --> 00:47:34.030
This is really the episode where David and I became such good friends.
这一集确实是大卫和我成为好朋友的契机。

1272
00:47:34.170 --> 00:47:36.230
Well, you had a lot of like St. Louis connections.
嗯，你们有很多像圣路易斯那样的联系。

1273
00:47:36.430 --> 00:47:36.730
We did.
确实有。

1274
00:47:37.090 --> 00:47:37.390
You had mutual friends.
你们有共同的朋友。

1275
00:47:37.550 --> 00:47:39.350
And we had the poker connection.
而且我们还有扑克牌局的交情。

1276
00:47:39.590 --> 00:47:40.030
Yes.
没错。

1277
00:47:40.270 --> 00:47:43.690
David and I played in a poker game together with our crew.
大卫和我曾和我们的剧组人员一起玩扑克。

1278
00:47:43.990 --> 00:47:45.550
We would host these poker games.
我们会组织这些扑克局。

1279
00:47:45.690 --> 00:47:46.710
Rain was in on it.
雷恩也参与其中。

1280
00:47:47.290 --> 00:47:49.850
Chris Workman, who was one of our camera operators.
还有我们的摄影师之一，克里斯·沃克曼。

1281
00:47:50.690 --> 00:47:52.270
Ed, our camera assistant.
我们的摄影助理埃德。

1282
00:47:52.390 --> 00:47:55.050
We would all get together and we would play poker.
我们大家会聚在一起打扑克。

1283
00:47:55.490 --> 00:47:56.830
And he was part of that.
他也是其中的一员。

1284
00:47:56.950 --> 00:47:58.210
So, he was one of my poker pals.
所以，他是我的牌友之一。

1285
00:47:58.930 --> 00:48:04.890
And anyway, this was the episode where we really became friends because we got left in that truck.
总之，这一集就是我们真正成为朋友的契机，因为我们被留在了那辆卡车里。

1286
00:48:05.150 --> 00:48:06.130
You got stuck in that truck.
你们被困在那辆卡车里了。

1287
00:48:06.450 --> 00:48:07.070
Jenna, do you know what?
珍娜，你知道吗？

1288
00:48:07.130 --> 00:48:12.170
I'm seeing a theme here that you become really close friends with people that you are in a confined space with.
我发现了一个主题，那就是你总是会和那些与你处于封闭空间里的人成为挚友。

1289
00:48:12.230 --> 00:48:13.490
That I get stuck with.
就是那些和我被困在一起的人。

1290
00:48:13.890 --> 00:48:14.570
You're stuck on a bench.
你被困在长凳上。

1291
00:48:14.670 --> 00:48:15.730
I'll be Angela's best friend.
我会成为安吉拉最好的朋友。

1292
00:48:15.730 --> 00:48:16.730
I'm stuck in a truck.
我被困在卡车里。

1293
00:48:16.910 --> 00:48:17.770
David, let's play poker.
大卫，我们来打扑克吧。

1294
00:48:18.870 --> 00:48:20.770
Get stuck in an elevator with me.
跟我一起被困在电梯里吧。

1295
00:48:20.930 --> 00:48:22.470
And then you're going to be best friends.
然后你们就会成为最好的朋友。

1296
00:48:22.530 --> 00:48:23.390
Friends for life.
一辈子的好朋友。

1297
00:48:23.390 --> 00:48:25.390
I have my final note card.
我有最后一张笔记卡。

1298
00:48:25.690 --> 00:48:26.010
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1299
00:48:26.310 --> 00:48:26.710
Yes.
准备好了。

1300
00:48:27.050 --> 00:48:27.530
All right.
好的。

1301
00:48:27.950 --> 00:48:39.910
At around 21 minutes, 25 seconds, you see both Meredith, played by Kate Flannery, and Meredith, played by Henriette, in the same episode.
在大约21分25秒的时候，你会在同一集里同时看到凯特·弗兰纳里饰演的梅雷迪思，以及亨丽埃特饰演的梅雷迪思。

1302
00:48:39.930 --> 00:48:40.490
Yes!
没错！

1303
00:48:40.610 --> 00:48:41.810
You saw it, Angela!
你看到了，安吉拉！

1304
00:48:41.810 --> 00:48:42.070
Yes!
没错！

1305
00:48:42.170 --> 00:48:44.890
I saw it and I almost texted you.
我看到了，而且差点就给你发短信了。

1306
00:48:45.190 --> 00:48:46.610
Background expert.
背景专家。

1307
00:48:46.930 --> 00:48:50.510
But I thought, no, I'm going to wait and see if she sees it.
但我心想，不行，我要等等看她能不能发现。

1308
00:48:50.570 --> 00:48:52.170
Yes, this is a huge mistake.
是的，这是一个巨大的失误。

1309
00:48:52.170 --> 00:48:53.250
It's a huge mistake.
这确实是个大失误。

1310
00:48:53.390 --> 00:48:58.970
So basically, while Michael has this talking head, they want to show all these clips of different women in the office.
基本上，当迈克尔在进行单人访谈时，他们想展示办公室里不同女性的片段。

1311
00:48:58.970 --> 00:49:05.830
And they used, like, some footage from the pilot before Kate Flannery came on.
他们用了凯特·弗兰纳里加入之前试播集里的一些素材。

1312
00:49:05.910 --> 00:49:07.090
And it was Henriette as Meredith.
那是亨丽埃特饰演的梅雷迪思。

1313
00:49:07.270 --> 00:49:12.810
You have this montage that goes Kate Flannery to Henriette to Luanne, who played in the Annex.
你看到的蒙太奇镜头是从凯特·弗兰纳里切换到亨丽埃特，再到在附楼工作的卢安。

1314
00:49:12.870 --> 00:49:15.990
Who was one of our extras for a very long time, so that makes sense.
她做了我们很久的临时演员，所以这说得通。

1315
00:49:16.330 --> 00:49:19.290
I saw that and I got so excited for you.
我看到的时候为你感到特别兴奋。

1316
00:49:19.370 --> 00:49:20.410
I got so excited.
我太兴奋了。

1317
00:49:20.630 --> 00:49:21.470
Because you knew.
因为你知道。

1318
00:49:21.590 --> 00:49:22.910
I knew you were going to clock it.
我就知道你一定会发现的。

1319
00:49:22.910 --> 00:49:24.610
You knew I had my note card ready.
你确实知道我准备好了笔记卡。

1320
00:49:24.870 --> 00:49:27.650
I have a final little tidbit.
我还有一个最后的小花絮。

1321
00:49:27.890 --> 00:49:29.670
I have a Fisher tidbit.
我有一个关于费舍尔的小花絮。

1322
00:49:29.890 --> 00:49:30.730
The coffee maker.
那个咖啡机。

1323
00:49:30.930 --> 00:49:33.370
We never find out who won the coffee maker.
我们从来没交代到底是谁赢了咖啡机。

1324
00:49:33.550 --> 00:49:34.050
No.
没有。

1325
00:49:34.590 --> 00:49:36.890
I'm feeling like I need to know.
我感觉我必须得知道。

1326
00:49:37.070 --> 00:49:39.890
We never find out who won it and we never see it again.
我们从来没交代是谁赢的，之后也再没见过它。

1327
00:49:40.050 --> 00:49:41.090
We never see it again.
我们再也没见过它。

1328
00:49:42.070 --> 00:49:44.910
I asked Phil Shea because a fan wrote in.
我问了菲尔·谢伊，因为有粉丝写信来问。

1329
00:49:44.990 --> 00:49:47.190
They wanted to know, did any of us get to keep it?
他们想知道，我们中有人留下了它吗？

1330
00:49:47.290 --> 00:49:50.270
People are very interested in the things we're allowed to keep and not keep.
大家对我们能留下什么、不能留下什么非常感兴趣。

1331
00:49:50.410 --> 00:49:50.850
I get it.
我理解。

1332
00:49:51.470 --> 00:49:52.670
He said no.
他说没有。

1333
00:49:53.090 --> 00:49:57.690
He said it was borrowed from Starbucks and had to be returned.
他说那是从星巴克借来的，必须归还。

1334
00:49:58.150 --> 00:49:59.150
I believe that.
我相信这一点。

1335
00:49:59.150 --> 00:50:00.570
Where is that machine now?
那台机器现在在哪儿呢？

1336
00:50:00.570 --> 00:50:01.750
I actually believe that.
我确实相信这一点。

1337
00:50:01.890 --> 00:50:06.150
And I bet the purses were returned because we were on a tight budget and we thought we
我敢打赌那些包也都还回去了，因为我们当时预算很紧，而且我们以为

1338
00:50:06.150 --> 00:50:06.990
were getting canceled.
我们会被砍掉。

1339
00:50:07.190 --> 00:50:07.350
Yes.
是的。

1340
00:50:07.450 --> 00:50:10.870
And we didn't want to give NBC any reason to think we were trouble.
我们不想给NBC任何理由认为我们是个麻烦。

1341
00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:11.770
That's right.
没错。

1342
00:50:11.770 --> 00:50:15.950
So I think I believe that all of that was returned and we got to recoup that money.
所以我认为我相信所有东西都归还了，我们得以收回那笔钱。

1343
00:50:16.110 --> 00:50:16.830
For sure.
肯定的。

1344
00:50:17.310 --> 00:50:20.070
Well, Jenna, I think that was some really fun fast facts.
好吧，珍娜，我觉得这些快速事实真的很有趣。

1345
00:50:20.170 --> 00:50:21.270
You did a great job.
你做得太棒了。

1346
00:50:21.270 --> 00:50:21.950
Wow.
哇。

1347
00:50:22.130 --> 00:50:22.610
Thank you.
谢谢。

1348
00:50:23.110 --> 00:50:23.910
You're welcome.
不客气。

1349
00:50:24.250 --> 00:50:25.810
I really appreciate it, Angela.
我真的很感激，安吉拉。

1350
00:50:26.130 --> 00:50:26.180
Oh, no.
噢，别这样。

1351
00:50:26.180 --> 00:50:26.450
No.
不。

1352
00:50:26.630 --> 00:50:27.210
I think.
我想是吧。

1353
00:50:27.350 --> 00:50:32.570
Now I need to hear you sing because if that's what you sound like, I just realized we've
现在我得听听你唱歌，因为如果这就是你的嗓音，我才意识到我们

1354
00:50:32.570 --> 00:50:35.210
never done karaoke or anything together.
从来没一起去唱过卡拉OK什么的。

1355
00:50:35.490 --> 00:50:42.370
On the wings of love, only the two of us together fly and hide.
在爱的羽翼上，只有我们两人一起飞翔躲藏。

1356
00:50:42.550 --> 00:50:43.330
Okay, don't sing anymore.
好了，别再唱了。

1357
00:50:43.330 --> 00:50:44.290
We'll have to pay for it.
我们得为此买单。

1358
00:50:45.650 --> 00:50:50.450
But now I know you're, now I have got your karaoke voice and it's whispery.
但现在我知道了，现在我有你的卡拉OK嗓了，是那种耳语般的唱法。

1359
00:50:50.450 --> 00:50:53.110
Well, I'm trying to cover up my floss.
嗯，我是在试图掩盖我的牙线。

1360
00:50:53.430 --> 00:50:56.070
And if you can't really sing, you whisper sing.
如果你真的不会唱歌，你就会用耳语来唱。

1361
00:50:56.610 --> 00:50:57.810
And that was Hot Girl.
刚才那是《辣妹》。

1362
00:50:58.010 --> 00:50:59.390
And that wraps up season one.
第一季到此结束。

1363
00:50:59.550 --> 00:51:01.970
Season one, where you and I become best friends.
第一季，你和我成为了最好的朋友。

1364
00:51:01.970 --> 00:51:02.270
Yes.
是的。

1365
00:51:02.470 --> 00:51:03.970
Because you were stuck on a bench with me.
因为你被困在长椅上和我在一起。

1366
00:51:04.150 --> 00:51:04.330
Yeah.
是啊。

1367
00:51:04.510 --> 00:51:07.070
And where you also became friends with someone because you were stuck in a car with them.
还有你和某人成为了朋友，因为你被困在车里和他们在一起。

1368
00:51:07.250 --> 00:51:07.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1369
00:51:07.590 --> 00:51:08.410
See a pattern here.
看出规律了吗。

1370
00:51:08.930 --> 00:51:10.390
What's going to happen season two?
第二季会发生什么呢？

1371
00:51:10.590 --> 00:51:13.030
Who do I get stuck with in season two?
第二季我会和谁被困在一起？

1372
00:51:13.550 --> 00:51:14.150
Dun, dun, dun.
当当当。

1373
00:51:14.770 --> 00:51:17.810
Speaking of season two, we are going to start with the Dundies.
说到第二季，我们将从“邓迪奖”那集开始。

1374
00:51:17.930 --> 00:51:18.670
Oh, I can't wait.
噢，我等不及了。

1375
00:51:18.810 --> 00:51:19.730
That's a big episode.
那可是个大制作的剧集。

1376
00:51:19.730 --> 00:51:21.430
A very, very big episode.
非常、非常重要的一集。

1377
00:51:21.690 --> 00:51:22.070
All right.
好的。

1378
00:51:22.150 --> 00:51:23.050
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1379
00:51:23.210 --> 00:51:23.970
See you next week.
下周见。

